s_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whatisboom/boom-ui/commit/cac93482440985f9c868660c853ead689eb688df","node_id":"C_kwDOQtUQc9oAKGNhYzkzNDgyNDQwOTg1ZjljODY4NjYwYzg1M2VhZDY4OWViNjg4ZGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whatisboom/boom-ui/commit/56148b3eaf6fa966a890b4c165268890d6faab4d","sha":"56148b3eaf6fa966a890b4c165268890d6faab4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whatisboom/boom-ui/commits/56148b3eaf6fa966a890b4c165268890d6faab4d"}],"sha":"cac93482440985f9c868660c853ead689eb688df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whatisboom/boom-ui/commits/cac93482440985f9c868660c853ead689eb688df"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/123084?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/whatisboom","id":123084,"login":"whatisboom","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMzA4NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whatisboom/boom-ui/commits/56148b3eaf6fa966a890b4c165268890d6faab4d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-19T01:54:17Z","email":"brandon@whatisboom.com","name":"Brandon Jernigan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-19T01:54:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: design identity overhaul - motion tokens, Sora font, shadow scale (#108)\n\n* Release v0.6.1 (#59)\n\n* Add Storybook deployment to GitHub Pages (#57)\n\n* Add GitHub Actions workflow for Storybook deployment to GitHub Pages\n\n* Use Node.js 24 and npm 11 to match project standards\n\n* Remove unnecessary memory options\n\n* Bump version to 0.6.1\n\n* Add Storybook deployment to GitHub Pages (#57)\n\n* Add GitHub Actions workflow for Storybook deployment to GitHub Pages\n\n* Use Node.js 24 and npm 11 to match project standards\n\n* Remove unnecessary memory options\n\n* Fix UI component issues: Avatar, Alert, Table pagination (#60)\n\n* Fix Avatar status indicator clipping by overflow\n\nThe status indicator was being cut off because the avatar container\nhad overflow: hidden to maintain circular shape. Implemented wrapper\nelement pattern: outer wrapper allows overflow while inner container\nclips the image to circular shape. Status indicator now renders fully.\n\n* Add colored left border to Alert component without icons\n\nAlerts with icon={null} now display a 4px colored left border matching\ntheir variant (info, success, warning, error) to provide visual\ndistinction. Previously, alerts without icons had no variant indicator.\n\n* Fix sticky table header by removing overflow when enabled\n\nPosition sticky requires no overflow between the sticky element and its\nscrolling ancestor. When stickyHeader is true, remove overflow from\ntableContainer so the header can stick. Users provide their own\nscrolling container (as shown in Storybook example).\n\n* Fix table pagination initial state mismatch in stories\n\nChanged initial pageSize from 5 to 10 in ClientSidePagination,\nManualPagination, and PaginationWithSortingAndSelection stories to\nmatch the default pageSizeOptions [10, 20, 50, 100]. Previously, the\ntable showed 5 rows while the dropdown displayed 10, causing confusion.\n\n* Fix table pagination layout and improve demo with 100 items\n\nAdded missing CSS classes that caused pagination buttons to stack\nvertically instead of staying horizontal:\n- .paginationNav: flex container for navigation buttons\n- .paginationPages: flex container for page number buttons\n- .paginationPageSize: flex container for rows-per-page selector\n- .paginationLabel: label styling\n- .paginationEllipsis: ellipsis styling\n\nAlso added responsive layout that stacks pagination vertically on\nmobile screens (<768px) and increased ClientSidePagination story\ndataset from 12 to 100 items to better demonstrate pagination.\n\nFixed class name: paginationSelect -> pageSizeSelect\n\n* Remove feature branch from PR checks workflow push trigger\n\nPrevents duplicate workflow runs when pushing to feature branches with\nopen PRs. The workflow was triggering on both push and pull_request\nevents, causing the same checks to run twice.\n\n* Add test coverage for CSS classes and wrapper structure\n\nAddresses Copilot review suggestions:\n- Alert: Add test verifying noIcon and variant CSS classes applied\n- Avatar: Add test verifying wrapper structure with status indicator\n  positioned outside avatar container to prevent clipping\n\nBoth tests verify the structural changes made to fix UI issues.\n\n* Add JSDoc documentation for stickyHeader prop requirement\n\nDocuments that users must provide their own scrolling container when\nusing stickyHeader. Includes example showing proper usage with a\ncontainer that has overflow: auto.\n\nAddresses Copilot review suggestion.\n\n* Fix release workflow to merge main to develop\n\n- Change auto-release workflow to merge main → develop instead of release branch → develop\n- Fixes race condition where release branch may be deleted before merge\n- Main always exists and contains the authoritative released state\n- Update branch deletion to handle already-deleted branches gracefully\n- Update conflict PR messages to clarify main → develop merge strategy\n- Update CLAUDE.md documentation to reflect new workflow\n\n* Bump version to 0.7.0\n\n* Fix workflow: use full git history for merge operations\n\n- Change fetch-depth from 2 to 0 to fetch full history\n- Fixes ''refusing to merge unrelated histories'' error\n- Git needs sufficient history to find common ancestor when merging main to develop\n\n* Bump version to 0.7.1\n\n* Fix checkbox vertical shift by stabilizing DOM structure\n\nChanged checkmark SVG from conditionally rendered to always rendered\nbut conditionally visible using CSS opacity. This prevents layout\nrecalculation when toggling checked state, eliminating vertical shift\nof content below the checkbox.\n\n- Remove conditional rendering of SVG element\n- Add CSS rule to hide checkmark with opacity: 0 when unchecked\n- Matches stable rendering pattern used by Switch component\n\n* Fix TableHeaderCell test to check specifically for SortIndicator\n\nUpdated test to look for SortIndicator class instead of any SVG element.\nThis prevents false positives from the Checkbox checkmark SVG which is\nnow always present in the DOM (just hidden with opacity when unchecked).\n\n* Fix Storybook backgrounds to respect theme tokens\n\nRemove hardcoded colors from Storybook configuration and let CSS tokens\ncontrol all theming. This ensures Storybook reflects custom theme values.\n\nChanges:\n- Remove hardcoded backgroundColor from ThemeDecorator\n- Remove all inline color manipulation from DocsContainer (~80 lines)\n- Remove redundant background addon configuration from preview.ts\n- Add storybook-theme.css with token-based styles for Storybook UI\n- Add --boom-theme-primary-text token for better contrast\n- Update Button outline/ghost/link variants to use primary-text token\n- Adjust Switch padding and positioning for better alignment\n- Update base palette hue to 50 (warm brown-gray) with adjusted saturation\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix conditional head parameter in PR creation\n\nUse release branch for conflict scenarios and main for push_failed scenarios to ensure semantic consistency with PR descriptions.\n\n* chore(deps-dev): bump lodash\n\nBumps the npm_and_yarn group with 1 update in the / directory: [lodash](https://github.com/lodash/lodash).\n\n\nUpdates `lodash` from 4.17.21 to 4.17.23\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/lodash/lodash/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/lodash/lodash/compare/4.17.21...4.17.23)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: lodash\n  dependency-version: 4.17.23\n  dependency-type: indirect\n  dependency-group: npm_and_yarn\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\n\n* Bump version to 0.7.2\n\n* feat(chart): install recharts and create file structure\n\n* feat(chart): define TypeScript interfaces\n\n* test(chart): add failing tests for color palette utility\n\n* feat(chart): implement color palette generation utility\n\n* style(chart): add CSS module with theme integration\n\n* feat(chart): add Chart component skeleton with theme integration\n\n* test(chart): add basic rendering and accessibility tests\n\n* feat(chart): implement line chart type with tests\n\n* feat(chart): implement bar, area, pie, and radar chart types with tests\n\n* feat(chart): add component exports\n\n* feat(chart): export Chart component from library\n\n* docs(chart): add Storybook stories for all chart types\n\n* fix(chart): address lint errors and accessibility issues\n\n* fix(chart): address Copilot feedback - fix legend position mapping and height handling\n\n- Map legend position correctly for left/right (align) vs top/bottom (verticalAlign)\n- Parse percentage string heights properly instead of coercing to 300\n- Remove unnecessary type assertion that triggered lint error\n\nAddresses Copilot review comments on PR #94\n\n* fix(chart): forward tooltip formatter and restrict height to number\n\nAddress remaining PR #94 Copilot review feedback:\n- Forward tooltip.formatter to all 5 Recharts Tooltip instances\n- Update formatter type to match Recharts Formatter signature\n- Restrict height prop to number only, removing ambiguous string parsing\n- Add test for formatter forwarding\n\n* fix(deps): bump @isaacs/brace-expansion 5.0.0 to 5.0.1\n\nResolves high severity Uncontrolled Resource Consumption vulnerability\n(GHSA-7h2j-956f-4vf2).\n\n* fix(chart): address PR review round 2 feedback\n\n- Replace title with aria-describedby for reliable screen reader support\n- Fix parseHSL regex to handle decimal values from computed styles\n- Guard against empty colors array causing modulo-by-zero in mapSeriesToColors\n- Guard pie chart against missing data keys producing undefined values\n\n* fix(chart): handle RGB computed styles in color palette generation\n\ngetComputedStyle resolves CSS variables to RGB values, but parseHSL\nonly matched hsl() format, causing the theme-derived palette to always\nfall back to hardcoded colors. Add parseColor/parseRGB/rgbToHSL to\nhandle both formats.\n\n* fix(chart): address remaining Copilot review comments on PR #94\n\n- Merge partial config defaults for legend/tooltip/grid instead of replacing\n- Wire prefers-reduced-motion to Recharts animations via useMediaQuery\n- Apply custom colors to pie chart slices (was ignoring colors prop)\n- Pass xAxisKey to extractDataKeys so custom keys aren''t treated as series\n- Fix auto-release workflow set -e issue around git push | tee pipeline\n\n* chore(deps): bump framer-motion from 12.26.2 to 12.29.2 (#97)\n\nBumps [framer-motion](https://github.com/motiondivision/motion) from 12.26.2 to 12.29.2.\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/motiondivision/motion/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/motiondivision/motion/compare/v12.26.2...v12.29.2)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: framer-motion\n  dependency-version: 12.29.2\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-minor\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* chore(deps-dev): bump react and @types/react (#98)\n\n* chore(deps-dev): bump react and @types/react\n\nBumps [react](https://github.com/facebook/react/tree/HEAD/packages/react) and [@types/react](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/tree/HEAD/types/react). These dependencies needed to be updated together.\n\nUpdates `react` from 19.2.3 to 19.2.4\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/facebook/react/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/facebook/react/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/facebook/react/commits/v19.2.4/packages/react)\n\nUpdates `@types/react` from 19.2.8 to 19.2.10\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/commits/HEAD/types/react)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: react\n  dependency-version: 19.2.4\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n- dependency-name: \"@types/react\"\n  dependency-version: 19.2.10\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\n\n* Also bump react-dom to 19.2.4 to match react\n\nReact 19+ requires exact version matches between react and react-dom.\nDependabot only bumped react, leaving react-dom at 19.2.3.\n\n* Fix high severity vulnerability in @isaacs/brace-expansion\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Brandon Jernigan <brandon@whatisboom.com>\n\n* chore(deps-dev): bump @storybook/addon-vitest from 10.1.11 to 10.2.3 (#99)\n\n* chore(deps-dev): bump @storybook/addon-vitest from 10.1.11 to 10.2.3\n\nBumps [@storybook/addon-vitest](https://github.com/storybookjs/storybook/tree/HEAD/code/addons/vitest) from 10.1.11 to 10.2.3.\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/storybookjs/storybook/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/storybookjs/storybook/blob/next/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/storybookjs/storybook/commits/v10.2.3/code/addons/vitest)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: \"@storybook/addon-vitest\"\n  dependency-version: 10.2.3\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-minor\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\n\n* Also bump @storybook/react-vite to 10.2.3 and fix audit vulnerability\n\n@storybook/addon-vitest 10.2.3 requires matching storybook core\npackages. Also fixes high severity vulnerability in @isaacs/brace-expansion.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Brandon Jernigan <brandon@whatisboom.com>\n\n* Bump vitest ecosystem to 4.0.18 (#100)\n\nBumps vitest, @vitest/ui, @vitest/coverage-v8, and\n@vitest/browser-playwright from 4.0.17 to 4.0.18 together to satisfy\npeer dependency requirements.\n\nReplaces #95 and #96 which bumped packages individually.\n\n* Bump version to 0.8.0\n\n* Align dependency version ranges\n\nBump Storybook packages to ^10.2.3 to match @storybook/react-vite,\nand align react-dom devDep to ^19.2.3 to match react.\n\n* Regenerate lock file with cross-platform optional dependencies\n\n* feat(tokens): add motion system, swap to Sora font, update shadow scale\n\n- Replace flat transition tokens with timing curves (ease-out, ease-in,\n  ease-in-out), named durations, and stagger delay\n- Alias old transition tokens for backward compatibility\n- Swap primary font from DM Sans to Sora\n- Add display/label typographic mode weight tokens\n- Tighten letter-spacing-tight and widen letter-spacing-wide\n- Tint shadows with accent hue for visual identity\n- Increase shadow vertical offsets for more presence\n\n* feat(css): replace transition: all with explicit properties, use motion tokens\n\n- Replace transition: all with explicit property lists in Button, Input,\n  Card, Switch, Checkbox, RadioGroup, NavItem, FormStepper, Audio, Image,\n  and Theme.stories\n- Replace hardcoded 0.2s/0.3s ease timings with motion token references\n- Replace hardcoded rgba() shadows in Switch and Checkbox with token refs\n\n* docs: update CLAUDE.md with motion tokens and Sora font guidance\n\n* feat(css): replace remaining hardcoded timings with motion tokens\n\nUpdate Breadcrumbs, Select, Tabs, and Textarea to use motion token\nreferences instead of hardcoded 0.2s ease values.\n\n* docs: add architecture, git-workflow, and patterns documentation\n\n* fix: restore eslint-disable comments for compound component patterns\n\n* fix(Chart): address PR review feedback from Copilot\n\n- Resolve CSS var() references in generateChartPalette via temporary DOM\n  element so theme colors are properly parsed instead of always falling\n  back to the hardcoded palette\n- Replace <span hidden> with <span className=\"sr-only\"> for aria-describedby\n  so screen readers can access the chart description\n- Replace hardcoded pie fill=\"#8884d8\" with first theme palette color\n\n* Update docs/architecture.md\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <175728472+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <175728472+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"3c2c33a8f9c7b8e44ebb3de152c00147de03f3aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whatisboom/boom-ui/git/trees/3c2c33a8f9c7b8e44ebb3de152c00147de03f3aa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whatisboom/boom-ui/git/commits/56148b3eaf6fa966a890b4c165268890d6faab4d","verification":{"payload":"tree 3c2c33a8f9c7b8e44ebb3de152c00147de03f3aa\nparent 96de470f2c4884dbae28403eb720833de9075064\nauthor Brandon Jernigan <brandon@whatisboom.com> 1773885257 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1773885257 -0500\n\nfeat: design identity overhaul - motion tokens, Sora font, shadow scale (#108)\n\n* Release v0.6.1 (#59)\n\n* Add Storybook deployment to GitHub Pages (#57)\n\n* Add GitHub Actions workflow for Storybook deployment to GitHub Pages\n\n* Use Node.js 24 and npm 11 to match project standards\n\n* Remove unnecessary memory options\n\n* Bump version to 0.6.1\n\n* Add Storybook deployment to GitHub Pages (#57)\n\n* Add GitHub Actions workflow for Storybook deployment to GitHub Pages\n\n* Use Node.js 24 and npm 11 to match project standards\n\n* Remove unnecessary memory options\n\n* Fix UI component issues: Avatar, Alert, Table pagination (#60)\n\n* Fix Avatar status indicator clipping by overflow\n\nThe status indicator was being cut off because the avatar container\nhad overflow: hidden to maintain circular shape. Implemented wrapper\nelement pattern: outer wrapper allows overflow while inner container\nclips the image to circular shape. Status indicator now renders fully.\n\n* Add colored left border to Alert component without icons\n\nAlerts with icon={null} now display a 4px colored left border matching\ntheir variant (info, success, warning, error) to provide visual\ndistinction. Previously, alerts without icons had no variant indicator.\n\n* Fix sticky table header by removing overflow when enabled\n\nPosition sticky requires no overflow between the sticky element and its\nscrolling ancestor. When stickyHeader is true, remove overflow from\ntableContainer so the header can stick. Users provide their own\nscrolling container (as shown in Storybook example).\n\n* Fix table pagination initial state mismatch in stories\n\nChanged initial pageSize from 5 to 10 in ClientSidePagination,\nManualPagination, and PaginationWithSortingAndSelection stories to\nmatch the default pageSizeOptions [10, 20, 50, 100]. Previously, the\ntable showed 5 rows while the dropdown displayed 10, causing confusion.\n\n* Fix table pagination layout and improve demo with 100 items\n\nAdded missing CSS classes that caused pagination buttons to stack\nvertically instead of staying horizontal:\n- .paginationNav: flex container for navigation buttons\n- .paginationPages: flex container for page number buttons\n- .paginationPageSize: flex container for rows-per-page selector\n- .paginationLabel: label styling\n- .paginationEllipsis: ellipsis styling\n\nAlso added responsive layout that stacks pagination vertically on\nmobile screens (<768px) and increased ClientSidePagination story\ndataset from 12 to 100 items to better demonstrate pagination.\n\nFixed class name: paginationSelect -> pageSizeSelect\n\n* Remove feature branch from PR checks workflow push trigger\n\nPrevents duplicate workflow runs when pushing to feature branches with\nopen PRs. The workflow was triggering on both push and pull_request\nevents, causing the same checks to run twice.\n\n* Add test coverage for CSS classes and wrapper structure\n\nAddresses Copilot review suggestions:\n- Alert: Add test verifying noIcon and variant CSS classes applied\n- Avatar: Add test verifying wrapper structure with status indicator\n  positioned outside avatar container to prevent clipping\n\nBoth tests verify the structural changes made to fix UI issues.\n\n* Add JSDoc documentation for stickyHeader prop requirement\n\nDocuments that users must provide their own scrolling container when\nusing stickyHeader. Includes example showing proper usage with a\ncontainer that has overflow: auto.\n\nAddresses Copilot review suggestion.\n\n* Fix release workflow to merge main to develop\n\n- Change auto-release workflow to merge main → develop instead of release branch → develop\n- Fixes race condition where release branch may be deleted before merge\n- Main always exists and contains the authoritative released state\n- Update branch deletion to handle already-deleted branches gracefully\n- Update conflict PR messages to clarify main → develop merge strategy\n- Update CLAUDE.md documentation to reflect new workflow\n\n* Bump version to 0.7.0\n\n* Fix workflow: use full git history for merge operations\n\n- Change fetch-depth from 2 to 0 to fetch full history\n- Fixes ''refusing to merge unrelated histories'' error\n- Git needs sufficient history to find common ancestor when merging main to develop\n\n* Bump version to 0.7.1\n\n* Fix checkbox vertical shift by stabilizing DOM structure\n\nChanged checkmark SVG from conditionally rendered to always rendered\nbut conditionally visible using CSS opacity. This prevents layout\nrecalculation when toggling checked state, eliminating vertical shift\nof content below the checkbox.\n\n- Remove conditional rendering of SVG element\n- Add CSS rule to hide checkmark with opacity: 0 when unchecked\n- Matches stable rendering pattern used by Switch component\n\n* Fix TableHeaderCell test to check specifically for SortIndicator\n\nUpdated test to look for SortIndicator class instead of any SVG element.\nThis prevents false positives from the Checkbox checkmark SVG which is\nnow always present in the DOM (just hidden with opacity when unchecked).\n\n* Fix Storybook backgrounds to respect theme tokens\n\nRemove hardcoded colors from Storybook configuration and let CSS tokens\ncontrol all theming. This ensures Storybook reflects custom theme values.\n\nChanges:\n- Remove hardcoded backgroundColor from ThemeDecorator\n- Remove all inline color manipulation from DocsContainer (~80 lines)\n- Remove redundant background addon configuration from preview.ts\n- Add storybook-theme.css with token-based styles for Storybook UI\n- Add --boom-theme-primary-text token for better contrast\n- Update Button outline/ghost/link variants to use primary-text token\n- Adjust Switch padding and positioning for better alignment\n- Update base palette hue to 50 (warm brown-gray) with adjusted saturation\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix conditional head parameter in PR creation\n\nUse release branch for conflict scenarios and main for push_failed scenarios to ensure semantic consistency with PR descriptions.\n\n* chore(deps-dev): bump lodash\n\nBumps the npm_and_yarn group with 1 update in the / directory: [lodash](https://github.com/lodash/lodash).\n\n\nUpdates `lodash` from 4.17.21 to 4.17.23\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/lodash/lodash/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/lodash/lodash/compare/4.17.21...4.17.23)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: lodash\n  dependency-version: 4.17.23\n  dependency-type: indirect\n  dependency-group: npm_and_yarn\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\n\n* Bump version to 0.7.2\n\n* feat(chart): install recharts and create file structure\n\n* feat(chart): define TypeScript interfaces\n\n* test(chart): add failing tests for color palette utility\n\n* feat(chart): implement color palette generation utility\n\n* style(chart): add CSS module with theme integration\n\n* feat(chart): add Chart component skeleton with theme integration\n\n* test(chart): add basic rendering and accessibility tests\n\n* feat(chart): implement line chart type with tests\n\n* feat(chart): implement bar, area, pie, and radar chart types with tests\n\n* feat(chart): add component exports\n\n* feat(chart): export Chart component from library\n\n* docs(chart): add Storybook stories for all chart types\n\n* fix(chart): address lint errors and accessibility issues\n\n* fix(chart): address Copilot feedback - fix legend position mapping and height handling\n\n- Map legend position correctly for left/right (align) vs top/bottom (verticalAlign)\n- Parse percentage string heights properly instead of coercing to 300\n- Remove unnecessary type assertion that triggered lint error\n\nAddresses Copilot review comments on PR #94\n\n* fix(chart): forward tooltip formatter and restrict height to number\n\nAddress remaining PR #94 Copilot review feedback:\n- Forward tooltip.formatter to all 5 Recharts Tooltip instances\n- Update formatter type to match Recharts Formatter signature\n- Restrict height prop to number only, removing ambiguous string parsing\n- Add test for formatter forwarding\n\n* fix(deps): bump @isaacs/brace-expansion 5.0.0 to 5.0.1\n\nResolves high severity Uncontrolled Resource Consumption vulnerability\n(GHSA-7h2j-956f-4vf2).\n\n* fix(chart): address PR review round 2 feedback\n\n- Replace title with aria-describedby for reliable screen reader support\n- Fix parseHSL regex to handle decimal values from computed styles\n- Guard against empty colors array causing modulo-by-zero in mapSeriesToColors\n- Guard pie chart against missing data keys producing undefined values\n\n* fix(chart): handle RGB computed styles in color palette generation\n\ngetComputedStyle resolves CSS variables to RGB values, but parseHSL\nonly matched hsl() format, causing the theme-derived palette to always\nfall back to hardcoded colors. Add parseColor/parseRGB/rgbToHSL to\nhandle both formats.\n\n* fix(chart): address remaining Copilot review comments on PR #94\n\n- Merge partial config defaults for legend/tooltip/grid instead of replacing\n- Wire prefers-reduced-motion to Recharts animations via useMediaQuery\n- Apply custom colors to pie chart slices (was ignoring colors prop)\n- Pass xAxisKey to extractDataKeys so custom keys aren''t treated as series\n- Fix auto-release workflow set -e issue around git push | tee pipeline\n\n* chore(deps): bump framer-motion from 12.26.2 to 12.29.2 (#97)\n\nBumps [framer-motion](https://github.com/motiondivision/motion) from 12.26.2 to 12.29.2.\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/motiondivision/motion/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/motiondivision/motion/compare/v12.26.2...v12.29.2)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: framer-motion\n  dependency-version: 12.29.2\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-minor\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* chore(deps-dev): bump react and @types/react (#98)\n\n* chore(deps-dev): bump react and @types/react\n\nBumps [react](https://github.com/facebook/react/tree/HEAD/packages/react) and [@types/react](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/tree/HEAD/types/react). These dependencies needed to be updated together.\n\nUpdates `react` from 19.2.3 to 19.2.4\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/facebook/react/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/facebook/react/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/facebook/react/commits/v19.2.4/packages/react)\n\nUpdates `@types/react` from 19.2.8 to 19.2.10\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/commits/HEAD/types/react)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: react\n  dependency-version: 19.2.4\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n- dependency-name: \"@types/react\"\n  dependency-version: 19.2.10\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\n\n* Also bump react-dom to 19.2.4 to match react\n\nReact 19+ requires exact version matches between react and react-dom.\nDependabot only bumped react, leaving react-dom at 19.2.3.\n\n* Fix high severity vulnerability in @isaacs/brace-expansion\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Brandon Jernigan <brandon@whatisboom.com>\n\n* chore(deps-dev): bump @storybook/addon-vitest from 10.1.11 to 10.2.3 (#99)\n\n* chore(deps-dev): bump @storybook/addon-vitest from 10.1.11 to 10.2.3\n\nBumps [@storybook/addon-vitest](https://github.com/storybookjs/storybook/tree/HEAD/code/addons/vitest) from 10.1.11 to 10.2.3.\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/storybookjs/storybook/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/storybookjs/storybook/blob/next/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/storybookjs/storybook/commits/v10.2.3/code/addons/vitest)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: \"@storybook/addon-vitest\"\n  dependency-version: 10.2.3\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-minor\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\n\n* Also bump @storybook/react-vite to 10.2.3 and fix audit vulnerability\n\n@storybook/addon-vitest 10.2.3 requires matching storybook core\npackages. Also fixes high severity vulnerability in @isaacs/brace-expansion.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Brandon Jernigan <brandon@whatisboom.com>\n\n* Bump vitest ecosystem to 4.0.18 (#100)\n\nBumps vitest, @vitest/ui, @vitest/coverage-v8, and\n@vitest/browser-playwright from 4.0.17 to 4.0.18 together to satisfy\npeer dependency requirements.\n\nReplaces #95 and #96 which bumped packages individually.\n\n* Bump version to 0.8.0\n\n* Align dependency version ranges\n\nBump Storybook packages to ^10.2.3 to match @storybook/react-vite,\nand align react-dom devDep to ^19.2.3 to match react.\n\n* Regenerate lock file with cross-platform optional dependencies\n\n* feat(tokens): add motion system, swap to Sora font, update shadow scale\n\n- Replace flat transition tokens with timing curves (ease-out, ease-in,\n  ease-in-out), named durations, and stagger delay\n- Alias old transition tokens for backward compatibility\n- Swap primary font from DM Sans to Sora\n- Add display/label typographic mode weight tokens\n- Tighten letter-spacing-tight and widen letter-spacing-wide\n- Tint shadows with accent hue for visual identity\n- Increase shadow vertical offsets for more presence\n\n* feat(css): replace transition: all with explicit properties, use motion tokens\n\n- Replace transition: all with explicit property lists in Button, Input,\n  Card, Switch, Checkbox, RadioGroup, NavItem, FormStepper, Audio, Image,\n  and Theme.stories\n- Replace hardcoded 0.2s/0.3s ease timings with motion token references\n- Replace hardcoded rgba() shadows in Switch and Checkbox with token refs\n\n* docs: update CLAUDE.md with motion tokens and Sora font guidance\n\n* feat(css): replace remaining hardcoded timings with motion tokens\n\nUpdate Breadcrumbs, Select, Tabs, and Textarea to use motion token\nreferences instead of hardcoded 0.2s ease values.\n\n* docs: add architecture, git-workflow, and patterns documentation\n\n* fix: restore eslint-disable comments for compound component patterns\n\n* fix(Chart): address PR review feedback from Copilot\n\n- Resolve CSS var() references in generateChartPalette via temporary DOM\n  element so theme colors are properly parsed instead of always falling\n  back to the hardcoded palette\n- Replace <span hidden> with <span className=\"sr-only\"> for aria-describedby\n  so screen readers can access the chart description\n- Replace hardcoded pie fill=\"#8884d8\" with first theme palette color\n\n* Update docs/architecture.md\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <175728472+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <175728472+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nw