5abe26990d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-01-28T02:29:31Z","email":"brandon@whatisboom.com","name":"Brandon Jernigan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-01-28T02:29:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Merge main to develop after v0.7.2 release (#93)\n\n* Release v0.6.1 (#59)\n\n* Add Storybook deployment to GitHub Pages (#57)\n\n* Add GitHub Actions workflow for Storybook deployment to GitHub Pages\n\n* Use Node.js 24 and npm 11 to match project standards\n\n* Remove unnecessary memory options\n\n* Bump version to 0.6.1\n\n* Add Storybook deployment to GitHub Pages (#57)\n\n* Add GitHub Actions workflow for Storybook deployment to GitHub Pages\n\n* Use Node.js 24 and npm 11 to match project standards\n\n* Remove unnecessary memory options\n\n* Fix UI component issues: Avatar, Alert, Table pagination (#60)\n\n* Fix Avatar status indicator clipping by overflow\n\nThe status indicator was being cut off because the avatar container\nhad overflow: hidden to maintain circular shape. Implemented wrapper\nelement pattern: outer wrapper allows overflow while inner container\nclips the image to circular shape. Status indicator now renders fully.\n\n* Add colored left border to Alert component without icons\n\nAlerts with icon={null} now display a 4px colored left border matching\ntheir variant (info, success, warning, error) to provide visual\ndistinction. Previously, alerts without icons had no variant indicator.\n\n* Fix sticky table header by removing overflow when enabled\n\nPosition sticky requires no overflow between the sticky element and its\nscrolling ancestor. When stickyHeader is true, remove overflow from\ntableContainer so the header can stick. Users provide their own\nscrolling container (as shown in Storybook example).\n\n* Fix table pagination initial state mismatch in stories\n\nChanged initial pageSize from 5 to 10 in ClientSidePagination,\nManualPagination, and PaginationWithSortingAndSelection stories to\nmatch the default pageSizeOptions [10, 20, 50, 100]. Previously, the\ntable showed 5 rows while the dropdown displayed 10, causing confusion.\n\n* Fix table pagination layout and improve demo with 100 items\n\nAdded missing CSS classes that caused pagination buttons to stack\nvertically instead of staying horizontal:\n- .paginationNav: flex container for navigation buttons\n- .paginationPages: flex container for page number buttons\n- .paginationPageSize: flex container for rows-per-page selector\n- .paginationLabel: label styling\n- .paginationEllipsis: ellipsis styling\n\nAlso added responsive layout that stacks pagination vertically on\nmobile screens (<768px) and increased ClientSidePagination story\ndataset from 12 to 100 items to better demonstrate pagination.\n\nFixed class name: paginationSelect -> pageSizeSelect\n\n* Remove feature branch from PR checks workflow push trigger\n\nPrevents duplicate workflow runs when pushing to feature branches with\nopen PRs. The workflow was triggering on both push and pull_request\nevents, causing the same checks to run twice.\n\n* Add test coverage for CSS classes and wrapper structure\n\nAddresses Copilot review suggestions:\n- Alert: Add test verifying noIcon and variant CSS classes applied\n- Avatar: Add test verifying wrapper structure with status indicator\n  positioned outside avatar container to prevent clipping\n\nBoth tests verify the structural changes made to fix UI issues.\n\n* Add JSDoc documentation for stickyHeader prop requirement\n\nDocuments that users must provide their own scrolling container when\nusing stickyHeader. Includes example showing proper usage with a\ncontainer that has overflow: auto.\n\nAddresses Copilot review suggestion.\n\n* Fix release workflow to merge main to develop\n\n- Change auto-release workflow to merge main → develop instead of release branch → develop\n- Fixes race condition where release branch may be deleted before merge\n- Main always exists and contains the authoritative released state\n- Update branch deletion to handle already-deleted branches gracefully\n- Update conflict PR messages to clarify main → develop merge strategy\n- Update CLAUDE.md documentation to reflect new workflow\n\n* Bump version to 0.7.0\n\n* Fix workflow: use full git history for merge operations\n\n- Change fetch-depth from 2 to 0 to fetch full history\n- Fixes ''refusing to merge unrelated histories'' error\n- Git needs sufficient history to find common ancestor when merging main to develop\n\n* Bump version to 0.7.1\n\n* Fix checkbox vertical shift by stabilizing DOM structure\n\nChanged checkmark SVG from conditionally rendered to always rendered\nbut conditionally visible using CSS opacity. This prevents layout\nrecalculation when toggling checked state, eliminating vertical shift\nof content below the checkbox.\n\n- Remove conditional rendering of SVG element\n- Add CSS rule to hide checkmark with opacity: 0 when unchecked\n- Matches stable rendering pattern used by Switch component\n\n* Fix TableHeaderCell test to check specifically for SortIndicator\n\nUpdated test to look for SortIndicator class instead of any SVG element.\nThis prevents false positives from the Checkbox checkmark SVG which is\nnow always present in the DOM (just hidden with opacity when unchecked).\n\n* Fix Storybook backgrounds to respect theme tokens\n\nRemove hardcoded colors from Storybook configuration and let CSS tokens\ncontrol all theming. This ensures Storybook reflects custom theme values.\n\nChanges:\n- Remove hardcoded backgroundColor from ThemeDecorator\n- Remove all inline color manipulation from DocsContainer (~80 lines)\n- Remove redundant background addon configuration from preview.ts\n- Add storybook-theme.css with token-based styles for Storybook UI\n- Add --boom-theme-primary-text token for better contrast\n- Update Button outline/ghost/link variants to use primary-text token\n- Adjust Switch padding and positioning for better alignment\n- Update base palette hue to 50 (warm brown-gray) with adjusted saturation\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix conditional head parameter in PR creation\n\nUse release branch for conflict scenarios and main for push_failed scenarios to ensure semantic consistency with PR descriptions.\n\n* chore(deps-dev): bump lodash\n\nBumps the npm_and_yarn group with 1 update in the / directory: [lodash](https://github.com/lodash/lodash).\n\n\nUpdates `lodash` from 4.17.21 to 4.17.23\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/lodash/lodash/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/lodash/lodash/compare/4.17.21...4.17.23)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: lodash\n  dependency-version: 4.17.23\n  dependency-type: indirect\n  dependency-group: npm_and_yarn\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\n\n* Bump version to 0.7.2\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"4e2676e6ed0ca140d0f73097ff8ad2ffc5a8e734","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whatisboom/boom-ui/git/trees/4e2676e6ed0ca140d0f73097ff8ad2ffc5a8e734"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whatisboom/boom-ui/git/commits/e6beac3342261e1f035d89e42304af5abe26990d","verification":{"payload":"tree 4e2676e6ed0ca140d0f73097ff8ad2ffc5a8e734\nparent 45eda5caac081d6b24f45cabf70a37ab7d2a7ddd\nauthor Brandon Jernigan <brandon@whatisboom.com> 1769567371 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1769567371 +0000\n\nMerge main to develop after v0.7.2 release (#93)\n\n* Release v0.6.1 (#59)\n\n* Add Storybook deployment to GitHub Pages (#57)\n\n* Add GitHub Actions workflow for Storybook deployment to GitHub Pages\n\n* Use Node.js 24 and npm 11 to match project standards\n\n* Remove unnecessary memory options\n\n* Bump version to 0.6.1\n\n* Add Storybook deployment to GitHub Pages (#57)\n\n* Add GitHub Actions workflow for Storybook deployment to GitHub Pages\n\n* Use Node.js 24 and npm 11 to match project standards\n\n* Remove unnecessary memory options\n\n* Fix UI component issues: Avatar, Alert, Table pagination (#60)\n\n* Fix Avatar status indicator clipping by overflow\n\nThe status indicator was being cut off because the avatar container\nhad overflow: hidden to maintain circular shape. Implemented wrapper\nelement pattern: outer wrapper allows overflow while inner container\nclips the image to circular shape. Status indicator now renders fully.\n\n* Add colored left border to Alert component without icons\n\nAlerts with icon={null} now display a 4px colored left border matching\ntheir variant (info, success, warning, error) to provide visual\ndistinction. Previously, alerts without icons had no variant indicator.\n\n* Fix sticky table header by removing overflow when enabled\n\nPosition sticky requires no overflow between the sticky element and its\nscrolling ancestor. When stickyHeader is true, remove overflow from\ntableContainer so the header can stick. Users provide their own\nscrolling container (as shown in Storybook example).\n\n* Fix table pagination initial state mismatch in stories\n\nChanged initial pageSize from 5 to 10 in ClientSidePagination,\nManualPagination, and PaginationWithSortingAndSelection stories to\nmatch the default pageSizeOptions [10, 20, 50, 100]. Previously, the\ntable showed 5 rows while the dropdown displayed 10, causing confusion.\n\n* Fix table pagination layout and improve demo with 100 items\n\nAdded missing CSS classes that caused pagination buttons to stack\nvertically instead of staying horizontal:\n- .paginationNav: flex container for navigation buttons\n- .paginationPages: flex container for page number buttons\n- .paginationPageSize: flex container for rows-per-page selector\n- .paginationLabel: label styling\n- .paginationEllipsis: ellipsis styling\n\nAlso added responsive layout that stacks pagination vertically on\nmobile screens (<768px) and increased ClientSidePagination story\ndataset from 12 to 100 items to better demonstrate pagination.\n\nFixed class name: paginationSelect -> pageSizeSelect\n\n* Remove feature branch from PR checks workflow push trigger\n\nPrevents duplicate workflow runs when pushing to feature branches with\nopen PRs. The workflow was triggering on both push and pull_request\nevents, causing the same checks to run twice.\n\n* Add test coverage for CSS classes and wrapper structure\n\nAddresses Copilot review suggestions:\n- Alert: Add test verifying noIcon and variant CSS classes applied\n- Avatar: Add test verifying wrapper structure with status indicator\n  positioned outside avatar container to prevent clipping\n\nBoth tests verify the structural changes made to fix UI issues.\n\n* Add JSDoc documentation for stickyHeader prop requirement\n\nDocuments that users must provide their own scrolling container when\nusing stickyHeader. Includes example showing proper usage with a\ncontainer that has overflow: auto.\n\nAddresses Copilot review suggestion.\n\n* Fix release workflow to merge main to develop\n\n- Change auto-release workflow to merge main → develop instead of release branch → develop\n- Fixes race condition where release branch may be deleted before merge\n- Main always exists and contains the authoritative released state\n- Update branch deletion to handle already-deleted branches gracefully\n- Update conflict PR messages to clarify main → develop merge strategy\n- Update CLAUDE.md documentation to reflect new workflow\n\n* Bump version to 0.7.0\n\n* Fix workflow: use full git history for merge operations\n\n- Change fetch-depth from 2 to 0 to fetch full history\n- Fixes ''refusing to merge unrelated histories'' error\n- Git needs sufficient history to find common ancestor when merging main to develop\n\n* Bump version to 0.7.1\n\n* Fix checkbox vertical shift by stabilizing DOM structure\n\nChanged checkmark SVG from conditionally rendered to always rendered\nbut conditionally visible using CSS opacity. This prevents layout\nrecalculation when toggling checked state, eliminating vertical shift\nof content below the checkbox.\n\n- Remove conditional rendering of SVG element\n- Add CSS rule to hide checkmark with opacity: 0 when unchecked\n- Matches stable rendering pattern used by Switch component\n\n* Fix TableHeaderCell test to check specifically for SortIndicator\n\nUpdated test to look for SortIndicator class instead of any SVG element.\nThis prevents false positives from the Checkbox checkmark SVG which is\nnow always present in the DOM (just hidden with opacity when unchecked).\n\n* Fix Storybook backgrounds to respect theme tokens\n\nRemove hardcoded colors from Storybook configuration and let CSS tokens\ncontrol all theming. This ensures Storybook reflects custom theme values.\n\nChanges:\n- Remove hardcoded backgroundColor from ThemeDecorator\n- Remove all inline color manipulation from DocsContainer (~80 lines)\n- Remove redundant background addon configuration from preview.ts\n- Add storybook-theme.css with token-based styles for Storybook UI\n- Add --boom-theme-primary-text token for better contrast\n- Update Button outline/ghost/link variants to use primary-text token\n- Adjust Switch padding and positioning for better alignment\n- Update base palette hue to 50 (warm brown-gray) with adjusted saturation\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix conditional head parameter in PR creation\n\nUse release branch for conflict scenarios and main for push_failed scenarios to ensure semantic consistency with PR descriptions.\n\n* chore(deps-dev): bump lodash\n\nBumps the npm_and_yarn group with 1 update in the / directory: [lodash](https://github.com/lodash/lodash).\n\n\nUpdates `lodash` from 4.17.21 to 4.17.23\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/lodash/lodash/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/lodash/lodash/compare/4.17.21...4.17.23)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: lodash\n  dependency-version: 4.17.23\n  dependency-type: indirect\n  dependency-group: npm_and_yarn\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\n\n* Bump version to 0.7.2\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpeXSLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAad8QABYUUaxwEId3fAQ7Hm//TWTN\nz4rZ6txIpYkwPyYFhI2XcufGjk3KImBbPabkptmZk7jyrchSRDLPoVfl/PY536zR\nf9ZfPEJ2Avrm2rpaQrYhbxdyQC9x8z7u9maO63JmcXT7xRGnL/32s80pprf2EXRF\npvS46Djw4c8rWByQOzr6zIiw73/p5MMVIejYHbFpG6e5LrERl/BNvs+jXzADOgBj\nxzWffu94gCUHI3S5gK7JpcGnghuaxKsK+5gFKBsKxM1kXxHZtizshl2YBTNdKr0x\nqIR7sanK+5NJ4mUD3uIJVafEyOW5LRnsC8TDrXJxTKykZwstVnSDebvF5rM29tOW\nu1lbhALr2xRNT8RG3ilLVB69FWraHGsUfDmjbOyU/zMrzjA7LucUUrCccggctkSI\nkvnEzbmwYiVgoMEFY+yCfjPk0FC4HPvBB0itACpL+8YIS9bWL60nLyMWuVm7H46v\ns3oa8x90CEouEGlVhPM6po0wYxTD5ZBQxUlhO+0hAb/FmdqRH+imHDlDrYXu2Tfb\nLCejDQkJyTxTz3uNifxiQs55FttXO2vazxuI1YbrfUq8WUsFSylq2KONjOMPDwby\ncjNZPwAjFI6q5vXz9anZuEuBXGHjLk8OtjfV2WsE1LYiG3E06Lr7/phQoT4qF3ZE\nA/lC1kqw9gvd0Z1wB0KS\n=6LvY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-01-28T02:29:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whatisboom/boom-ui/commit/e6beac3342261e1f035d89e42304af5abe26990d","node_id":"C_kwDOQtUQc9oAKGU2YmVhYzMzNDIyNjFlMWYwMzVkODllNDIzMDRhZjVhYmUyNjk5MGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whatisboom/boom-ui/commit/45eda5caac081d6b24f45cabf70a37ab7d2a7ddd","sha":"45eda5caac081d6b24f45cabf70a37ab7d2a7ddd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whatisboom/boom-ui/commits/45eda5caac081d6b24f45cabf70a37ab7d2a7ddd"}],"sha":"e6beac3342261e1f035d89e42304af5abe26990d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whatisboom/boom-ui/commits/e6beac3342261e1f035d89e42304af5abe26990d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/123084?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/whatisboom","id":123084,"login":"whatisboom","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMzA4NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whatisboom/boom-ui/commits/45eda5caac081d6b24f45cabf70a37ab7d2a7ddd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-01-28T02:22:54Z","email":"brandon@whatisboom.com","name":"Brandon Jernigan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-01-28T02:22:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix git push exit code detection in auto-release workflow (#92)\n\n* Fix git push exit code detection in auto-release workflow\n\nThe workflow was using `git push | tee` which causes the shell to\ncapture tee''s exit code (always 0) instead of git push''s actual exit\ncode. This prevented the workflow from detecting when pushes failed\ndue to branch protection rules.\n\nFix by capturing PIPESTATUS[0] before checking exit code, which\ncontains the actual exit code of git push (first command in pipeline).\n\nThis ensures the workflow correctly:\n- Detects when push to develop fails\n- Sets merge_status=push_failed appropriately\n- Triggers auto-PR creation for manual conflict resolution\n- Prevents premature deletion of release branches\n\n* Address Copilot review feedback\n\n- Add explicit shell: bash to ensure PIPESTATUS works correctly\n- Remove duplicate cat of push_output.log (tee already streams to logs)","tree":{"sha":"35e67bd0f70cf9aaf0bacff99e56233ced0496ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whatisboom/boom-ui/git/trees/35e67bd0f70cf9aaf0bacff99e56233ced0496ab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whatisboom/boom-ui/git/commits/45eda5caac081d6b24f45cabf70a37ab7d2a7ddd","verification":{"payload":"tree 35e67bd0f70cf9aaf0bacff99e56233ced0496ab\nparent a322dda524e7739a023b86925acfd9c911f20764\nauthor Brandon Jernigan <brandon@whatisboom.com> 1769566974 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1769566974 +0000\n\nFix git push exit code detection in auto-release workflow (#92)\n\n* Fix git push exit code detection in auto-release workflow\n\nThe workflow was using `git push | tee` which causes the shell to\ncapture tee''s exit code (always 0) instead of git push''s actual exit\ncode. This prevented the workflow from detecting when pushes failed\ndue to branch protection rules.\n\nFix by capturing PIPESTATUS[0] before checking exit code, which\ncontains the actual exit code of git push (first command in pipeline).\n\nThis ensures the workflow correctly:\n- Detects when push to develop fails\n- Sets merge_status=push_failed appropriately\n- Triggers auto-PR creation for manual conflict resolution\n- Prevents premature deletion of release branches\n\n* Address Copilot review feedback\n\n- Add explicit shell: bash to ensure PIPESTATUS works correctly\n- Remove duplicate cat of push_output.log (tee already streams to logs)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpeXL+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8K4QAIR4pv0wXXTv/J4HeF5OjTvp\nUXWspeAmuJrbCr9iWQS7U/gm1t5Plv20bP9UpegJTIWiMh002ychcHEMl9KphIL0\nGnYzcsnEA+Nwbty9WGMM5TA9FMj/xnNThqHVFElaSHYfBZvYEtPMkGcFrRvyxKv7\nF1+nXe1cPyuuKJRqCOo8GeAqcEBm6Er36AABrxZBJpo/ow0SSeoZ2NULj7Cz7q5S\n2Jw147yVUVQf8ag93zO+p5p7VluTM/JQVf/2Oj/lkyEuVk/IJgVFJU5LSJ/3yblH\n+vmi4OhX9p14v0e7enzwsTn7q+ekxKUFylGO2eOpBE+UezUKMPNSll9yklmUXgye\neHMSt9lDm6wXPRLBENCoxJCHRAxlmcThAcN1ByWdFW6eZr2SVDy8A2I2tcMSRjG9\nDn9JTfUpfxVPyCfcshmzCj3uQuJEiGVF+Z/nwBIhKIx9Zmag6SRK0ZNcYZ/Ppxxj\n9qxpnelEqX9MoyzM3NL3s+SAdaS8EIxFV67SkKL7s8aX949XVlxWO/GE422MpI7r\ndiYumZyKZa6uLMkpApA4nfvNh0jiRAU8BaEkzVCuJsFZOoWnemTEz8kIAG126kTz\nb3jnihQ7f6Udw6U/f5X6zax5AfUaRQcJMiXDxBfijTwEpinEdUHIAyiAUpHTbG39\nPhBZoxduPhNRhQJCchKg\n=+vzK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-01-28T02:22:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/or