hub.com/users/whatisboom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/whatisboom","id":123084,"login":"whatisboom","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMzA4NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whatisboom/boom-ui/commits/525e7a5c5d32a51bdad5b6d65a9ecc829dd5cb07/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-01-21T00:29:20Z","email":"brandon@whatisboom.com","name":"Brandon Jernigan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-01-21T00:29:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(layout): implement AppShell component and fix Storybook documentation (#73)\n\n* docs: map existing codebase\n\n- STACK.md - Technologies and dependencies\n- ARCHITECTURE.md - System design and patterns\n- STRUCTURE.md - Directory layout\n- CONVENTIONS.md - Code style and patterns\n- TESTING.md - Test structure\n- INTEGRATIONS.md - External services\n- CONCERNS.md - Technical debt and issues\n\n* feat(layout): implement AppShell component\n\nAdd AppShell layout component with optional header and sidebar using CSS Grid with named areas. Component provides flexible application structure with full viewport height and independent scrolling areas.\n\n- Create AppShell component with props-based API\n- Add comprehensive test suite (33 tests, all passing)\n- Include 8 Storybook stories demonstrating variants\n- Export Header component (previously missing from public API)\n- Support dynamic grid layout based on present components\n- Implement proper accessibility with ARIA roles\n- Follow TDD methodology (RED-GREEN-REFACTOR)\n\n* fix(storybook): configure TypeScript docgen for cleaner type display\n\n- Add typescript.reactDocgen config to use react-docgen-typescript\n- Enable docs.autodocs for automatic documentation\n- Prevents verbose file paths in type definitions (e.g., Size instead of import(''/path/to/file'').Size)\n\n* fix(storybook): configure source code display settings\n\n- Set docs.source.type to ''code'' to show story source instead of compiled output\n- Add excludeDecorators option to clean up code snippets\n- Configure TSX syntax highlighting for code examples\n- Apply source settings globally in preview.ts\n\n* fix(storybook): clean up AppShell args table display\n\nConfigure argTypes to hide React element props from controls and display clean type summaries instead of compiled JSX internals. Prevents verbose jsxDEV output with file paths in the documentation Args table.\n\n- Set control: false for header, sidebar, and children props\n- Override table.type.summary with clean type descriptions\n- Add helpful descriptions for each prop\n\n* fix(storybook): use dynamic source to show clean JSX\n\nChange source type from ''code'' to ''dynamic'' to show rendered JSX instead of story args object in ''Show code'' sections. Makes code examples cleaner and more copy-pasteable.\n\n* chore: remove .planning directory from git tracking\n\nAdd .planning/ to .gitignore to exclude planning/documentation files from version control. Files remain locally but are no longer tracked by git.\n\n* docs(AppShell): clarify grid layout property override behavior\n\nAdd documentation explaining that grid template properties are intentionally managed by the component and will override user-provided values. This is by design to ensure the layout structure is preserved based on header/sidebar presence.\n\nChanges:\n- Add code comment explaining property override order\n- Update style prop JSDoc to document grid property behavior\n\nAddresses: PR review comment about style prop spread order\n\n* fix(AppShell): allow users to override grid layout via style prop\n\nReverse property spread order to respect user customization. Users can now override the default grid template properties if they need advanced layout customization.\n\nChanges:\n- Move ...style spread after grid properties (was before)\n- Update documentation to reflect that grid layout CAN be overridden\n- Trusts users to know what they''re doing with advanced customization\n\nRationale: The previous implementation was too restrictive. If users want to customize the grid, they should be able to - it''s their responsibility to maintain a working layout.\n\n* feat(AppShell): support right-positioned sidebar and fix formatting\n\nAddress PR review comments:\n\n1. **Sidebar Position Support**: AppShell now respects the Sidebar''s position prop\n   - Extract sidebar position from sidebar?.props.position\n   - Adjust grid template areas for right-positioned sidebars\n   - Adjust grid template columns order (1fr then sidebarWidth for right position)\n   - Add 4 new tests covering left/right positioning scenarios (37 tests total)\n   - Add RightSidebar story demonstrating right-positioned layout\n\n2. **Formatting Fix**: Remove extra blank line in .storybook/main.ts for consistent spacing\n\nChanges:\n- AppShell now dynamically adjusts layout based on sidebar position\n- Grid areas: ''main sidebar'' for right position vs ''sidebar main'' for left\n- Grid columns: ''1fr 280px'' for right position vs ''280px 1fr'' for left\n- All 37 tests passing with 100% coverage maintained\n\nAddresses: GitHub Copilot review comments on PR #73\n\n* fix(AppShell): use grid auto-sizing for dynamic sidebar width\n\n- Use CSS Grid ''auto'' instead of fixed widths for sidebar columns\n- Grid now adapts automatically when sidebar collapses/expands\n- Fixes issue where collapsed sidebar left empty space in layout\n- Remove unused DEFAULT_SIDEBAR_WIDTH constant\n- Update test expectations to match new auto-sizing behavior\n- Fix misleading comment in .storybook/main.ts about type checking\n- Refactor FullApplication story to use layout components (Box, Stack, Grid, Card)\n  instead of inline styles for better consistency\n\nResolves Copilot review comments on collapsed sidebar state handling","tree":{"sha":"615cda16d41409d1ff3902a5c983043b2fd3cf32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whatisboom/boom-ui/git/trees/615cda16d41409d1ff3902a5c983043b2fd3cf32"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whatisboom/boom-ui/git/commits/525e7a5c5d32a51bdad5b6d65a9ecc829dd5cb07","verification":{"payload":"tree 615cda16d41409d1ff3902a5c983043b2fd3cf32\nparent 51cccee37407aa334a05b17f8ee60aff9e97c8bb\nauthor Brandon Jernigan <brandon@whatisboom.com> 1768955360 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1768955360 +0000\n\nfeat(layout): implement AppShell component and fix Storybook documentation (#73)\n\n* docs: map existing codebase\n\n- STACK.md - Technologies and dependencies\n- ARCHITECTURE.md - System design and patterns\n- STRUCTURE.md - Directory layout\n- CONVENTIONS.md - Code style and patterns\n- TESTING.md - Test structure\n- INTEGRATIONS.md - External services\n- CONCERNS.md - Technical debt and issues\n\n* feat(layout): implement AppShell component\n\nAdd AppShell layout component with optional header and sidebar using CSS Grid with named areas. Component provides flexible application structure with full viewport height and independent scrolling areas.\n\n- Create AppShell component with props-based API\n- Add comprehensive test suite (33 tests, all passing)\n- Include 8 Storybook stories demonstrating variants\n- Export Header component (previously missing from public API)\n- Support dynamic grid layout based on present components\n- Implement proper accessibility with ARIA roles\n- Follow TDD methodology (RED-GREEN-REFACTOR)\n\n* fix(storybook): configure TypeScript docgen for cleaner type display\n\n- Add typescript.reactDocgen config to use react-docgen-typescript\n- Enable docs.autodocs for automatic documentation\n- Prevents verbose file paths in type definitions (e.g., Size instead of import(''/path/to/file'').Size)\n\n* fix(storybook): configure source code display settings\n\n- Set docs.source.type to ''code'' to show story source instead of compiled output\n- Add excludeDecorators option to clean up code snippets\n- Configure TSX syntax highlighting for code examples\n- Apply source settings globally in preview.ts\n\n* fix(storybook): clean up AppShell args table display\n\nConfigure argTypes to hide React element props from controls and display clean type summaries instead of compiled JSX internals. Prevents verbose jsxDEV output with file paths in the documentation Args table.\n\n- Set control: false for header, sidebar, and children props\n- Override table.type.summary with clean type descriptions\n- Add helpful descriptions for each prop\n\n* fix(storybook): use dynamic source to show clean JSX\n\nChange source type from ''code'' to ''dynamic'' to show rendered JSX instead of story args object in ''Show code'' sections. Makes code examples cleaner and more copy-pasteable.\n\n* chore: remove .planning directory from git tracking\n\nAdd .planning/ to .gitignore to exclude planning/documentation files from version control. Files remain locally but are no longer tracked by git.\n\n* docs(AppShell): clarify grid layout property override behavior\n\nAdd documentation explaining that grid template properties are intentionally managed by the component and will override user-provided values. This is by design to ensure the layout structure is preserved based on header/sidebar presence.\n\nChanges:\n- Add code comment explaining property override order\n- Update style prop JSDoc to document grid property behavior\n\nAddresses: PR review comment about style prop spread order\n\n* fix(AppShell): allow users to override grid layout via style prop\n\nReverse property spread order to respect user customization. Users can now override the default grid template properties if they need advanced layout customization.\n\nChanges:\n- Move ...style spread after grid properties (was before)\n- Update documentation to reflect that grid layout CAN be overridden\n- Trusts users to know what they''re doing with advanced customization\n\nRationale: The previous implementation was too restrictive. If users want to customize the grid, they should be able to - it''s their responsibility to maintain a working layout.\n\n* feat(AppShell): support right-positioned sidebar and fix formatting\n\nAddress PR review comments:\n\n1. **Sidebar Position Support**: AppShell now respects the Sidebar''s position prop\n   - Extract sidebar position from sidebar?.props.position\n   - Adjust grid template areas for right-positioned sidebars\n   - Adjust grid template columns order (1fr then sidebarWidth for right position)\n   - Add 4 new tests covering left/right positioning scenarios (37 tests total)\n   - Add RightSidebar story demonstrating right-positioned layout\n\n2. **Formatting Fix**: Remove extra blank line in .storybook/main.ts for consistent spacing\n\nChanges:\n- AppShell now dynamically adjusts layout based on sidebar position\n- Grid areas: ''main sidebar'' for right position vs ''sidebar main'' for left\n- Grid columns: ''1fr 280px'' for right position vs ''280px 1fr'' for left\n- All 37 tests passing with 100% coverage maintained\n\nAddresses: GitHub Copilot review comments on PR #73\n\n* fix(AppShell): use grid auto-sizing for dynamic sidebar width\n\n- Use CSS Grid ''auto'' instead of fixed widths for sidebar columns\n- Grid now adapts automatically when sidebar collapses/expands\n- Fixes issue where collapsed sidebar left empty space in layout\n- Remove unused DEFAULT_SIDEBAR_WIDTH constant\n- Update test expectations to match new auto-sizing behavior\n- Fix misleading comment in .storybook/main.ts about type checking\n- Refactor FullApplication story to use layout components (Box, Stack, Grid, Card)\n  instead of inline styles for better consistency\n\nResolves Copilot review comments on collapsed sidebar state handling","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpcB3gCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOlIQAFy+D4LEqDB7DXq4lnYxYV96\nZfNumfkuEnOH86nLTd2W5oyCe01GlNa7i/IGpOagfqWVDoCMCB2UR/TSLU5Wl5lN\nEXtZneFtRpaqPxxVHT9JdUsg8YohBPiWMUitYdkjbzmfF3yKaaJISWybcwzb1eAe\n6av3p/qi6ANHd7INYVbSYA7GgahwlIXYWvwV73M5C5GBERBw4P/zxqgv6AAWmW8T\nAlfl5UQb8+0/GIFHZ4PMZW1H4rYxN/xnQm8B3L1iUbucUJqnEFEztePRC1f9zn0W\ntZUVVQcNLn1iQAzkUn3LSGIA5XHXA4kD1o1NyzQdEma6BcxELhcSvm/rvjYVckuW\nLs2TbRwV797uAx69B47I3ccx2QaauLAN5NEv1e6iHsZK86Wsab1Uf9sLUXSqhQuC\nU9KnMgoh6y4Eb64bnTkRbIg0dcmRCfPFDbsY1YSBb2Gu8QKRL0vnOBQaV5CyP0E5\nhc+uXgb6nhNm1v/z5F45onvHxwSTUpd8nrcmKQZi8dSBzZoThGCS3h2cKD64LHeG\nS3nLGCuDwiJsQ/drgh42S39lQN3AjNb+6S46YGLNF6xTKWT+EWPUC20+kmJxmaeq\n5Vx9eoSBqb1859GATNJzLaqs86QQt874U2BVXv/jv6WVC2se3sArXyDzlJLWKmih\nBqqqCSsL0rI17yLwI7uc\n=3xUI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-01-21T00:29:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whatisboom/boom-ui/commit/525e7a5c5d32a51bdad5b6d65a9ecc829dd5cb07","node_id":"C_kwDOQtUQc9oAKDUyNWU3YTVjNWQzMmE1MWJkYWQ1YjZkNjVhOWVjYzgyOWRkNWNiMDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whatisboom/boom-ui/commit/51cccee37407aa334a05b17f8ee60aff9e97c8bb","sha":"51cccee37407aa334a05b17f8ee60aff9e97c8bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whatisboom/boom-ui/commits/51cccee37407aa334a05b17f8ee60aff9e97c8bb"}],"sha":"525e7a5c5d32a51bdad5b6d65a9ecc829dd5cb07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whatisboom/boom-ui/commits/525e7a5c5d32a51bdad5b6d65a9ecc829dd5cb07"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/123084?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/whatisboom","id":123084,"login":"whatisboom","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMzA4NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whatisboom/boom-ui/commits/51cccee37407aa334a05b17f8ee60aff9e97c8bb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-01-20T04:41:44Z","email":"brandon@whatisboom.com","name":"Brandon Jernigan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-01-20T04:41:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: new components and improvements (#72)\n\n* feat(layout): implement Sidebar component\n\n- Add compound component pattern (Sidebar, Sidebar.Header, Sidebar.Nav, Sidebar.Item)\n- Support controlled and uncontrolled collapsed state\n- Implement rail mode (icon-only when collapsed)\n- Add responsive behavior (Drawer overlay on mobile, static on desktop)\n- Support left/right positioning\n- Add width customization\n- Implement smooth animations with Framer Motion\n- Add useMediaQuery hook for responsive breakpoint detection\n- Include comprehensive tests with 80%+ coverage\n- Add accessibility tests with vitest-axe\n- Create Storybook stories showing all variants\n\n* WIP: Auto-fixes from linter\n\n* More linter auto-fixes\n\n* fix: resolve TypeScript and lint errors\n\n- Fix Video and Audio Storybook imports to use react-vite\n- Fix Menu setItemCount type to use Dispatch\n- Fix Image test type assertions\n- Add Audio.utils.ts to extract formatTime helper\n- Add caption track to Audio element for accessibility\n- Add eslint-disable for Audio ref dependencies\n\n* fix: resolve all remaining lint errors\n\n- Remove useCallback from Menu handleKeyDown (React Compiler optimizes)\n- Remove unused useCallback import in MenuContent\n- Add eslint-disable for Audio ref immutability warnings\n- Fix Video caption track accessibility\n\n* fix(nav): improve active item contrast in dark mode\n\nActive nav items now use pure white text in dark mode for maximum\ncontrast, while light mode retains the brand blue color.\n\n* fix(video): prevent volume slider from being clipped\n\nChanged volumeSliderWrapper overflow from hidden to visible to allow\nthe slider handle to be fully visible when it extends beyond the track.\n\n* fix(navigation): improve active link contrast in dark mode\n\nActive navigation links now use pure white text in dark mode for\nmaximum contrast, while light mode retains the brand blue color.\n\n* fix(image): reset loading state when src changes\n\nAdded useEffect to reset loading and error states when image src prop\nchanges, ensuring proper loading indicator display for new images.\n\n* fix(skeleton): prevent inline style from overriding circle border-radius\n\nCircle variant now skips inline border-radius style to allow CSS class\nto apply 50% border-radius. Added test to verify this behavior.\n\n* fix(video): correct prop name in test\n\nFixed test to use correct prop name onVideoTimeUpdate instead of\nonTimeUpdate to match the component''s actual API.\n\n* refactor: remove Menu component\n\nRemoved Menu component as it has been replaced by other navigation\ncomponents in the library.\n\n* docs(storybook): reorganize component categories\n\nAdded story sorting order and reorganized all component stories into\nlogical categories: Getting Started, Layout, Core, Navigation, Forms,\nOverlays & Dialogs, Feedback & Status, Media, and Data Display.\n\n* refactor: remove Menu component exports from index\n\nRemoved Menu component exports after component deletion to fix\nTypeScript errors about missing module.\n\n* feat(video): improve volume slider UX with grace period\n\nAdded configurable delay (default 500ms) before hiding volume slider\nafter mouse leaves. Slider stays visible while actively dragging and\nprovides grace period for returning to adjust volume.\n\n- Added volumeSliderDelay prop to Video component\n- Implemented state management for slider visibility with timer\n- Slider remains visible during active drag interactions\n- Updated CSS to support programmatic visibility control\n- All existing tests pass\n\n* style(video): improve volume slider visibility and spacing\n\nAdded dark background and padding to volume slider when visible, and\nreduced gap between volume icon and slider for better visual grouping.\n\n* fix(audio): prevent volume slider from being clipped and improve styling\n\n- Added overflow: visible to controls, buttonGroup, and volumeControl\n  to prevent volume slider from being cut off\n- Reduced margin-bottom and padding for more compact appearance\n- Moved slider closer to volume icon for better visual proximity\n- Improved background with theme tokens and enhanced shadow\n- Reduced width from 120px to 100px for better proportions\n\n* style(audio): refine volume slider styling for dark theme\n\n- Removed vertical padding (kept horizontal only)\n- Added dark theme specific styles with darker background (85% black)\n  and subtle border (15% white) for better visual contrast\n\n* style(audio): increase volume slider horizontal padding\n\nIncreased horizontal padding from spacing-2 to spacing-4 to prevent\nslider indicator from getting too close to the edges.\n\n* feat(audio): add loop toggle control and fix CSS variables\n\n- Add loop toggle button with visual indicator (primary color when active)\n- Add state management for loop control in both single and playlist modes\n- Fix CSS variables throughout component (--boom-color-* to --boom-theme-*)\n- Update button styling to use color-only approach without backgrounds\n- Support playlist looping (restarts from first track after last track ends)\n\n* docs(audio): add visual styling to Custom Styled story\n\nAdd custom CSS decorator with pink/purple gradient theme to demonstrate\nclassName prop usage for custom theming. Previously the story had no\nvisual difference from the default story.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: resolve TypeScript and lint errors in Video and Image components\n\n- Video: Fix ref handling by using internal ref and merging with forwarded ref\n- Video: Fix PiP toggle to capture ref value before async operation\n- Image: Fix setState in useEffect with proper eslint suppression\n- VideoControls: Add eslint suppression for non-interactive div wrapper\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: resolve TypeScript type errors in FormStepper, NotificationMenu, and Video components\n\n- Add type guard function in FormStepper to properly narrow React children to FormStep elements\n- Update NotificationMenu context to accept nullable button ref\n- Update Video component refs to properly reflect nullable types\n- Remove unnecessary type assertions and simplify code\n\nThese changes fix CI type check and lint failures while maintaining type safety.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"49796667df2064a18e93d8e3685aac0a7d35970e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whatisboom/boom-ui/git/trees/49796667df2064a18e93d8e3685aac0a7d35970e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whatisboom/boom-ui/git/commits/51cccee37407aa334a05b17f8ee60aff9e97c8bb","verification":{"payload":"tree 49796667df2064a18e93d8e3685aac0a7d35970e\nparent 1a5a137f0ad599d30c1b2ea52da154ccbee07c4b\nauthor Brandon Jernigan <brandon@whatisboom.com> 1768884104 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1768884104 -0600\n\nfeat: new components and improvements (#72)\n\n* feat(layout): implement Sidebar component\n\n- Add compound component pattern (Sidebar, Sidebar.Header, Sidebar.Nav, Sidebar.Item)\n- Support controlled and uncontrolled collapsed state\n- Implement rail mode (icon-only when collapsed)\n- Add responsive behavior (Drawer overlay on mobile, static on desktop)\n- Support left/right positioning\n- Add width customization\n- Implement smooth animations with Framer Motion\n- Add useMediaQuery hook for responsive breakpoint detection\n- Include comprehensive tests with 80%+ coverage\n- Add accessibility tests with vitest-axe\n- Create Storybook stories showing all variants\n\n* WIP: Auto-fixes from linter\n\n* More linter auto-fixes\n\n* fix: resolve TypeScript and lint errors\n\n- Fix Video and Audio Storybook imports to use react-vite\n- Fix Menu setItemCount type to use Dispatch\n- Fix Image test type assertions\n- Add Audio.utils.ts to extract formatTime helper\n- Add caption track to Audio element for accessibility\n- Add eslint-disable for Audio ref dependencies\n\n* fix: resolve all remaining lint errors\n\n- Remove useCallback from Menu handleKeyDown (React Compiler optimizes)\n- Remove unused useCallback import in MenuContent\n- Add eslint-disable for Audio ref immutability warnings\n- Fix Video caption track accessibility\n\n* fix(nav): improve active item contrast in dark mode\n\nActive nav items now use pure white text in dark mode for maximum\ncontrast, while light mode retains the brand blue color.\n\n* fix(video): prevent volume slider from being clipped\n\nChanged volumeSliderWrapper overflow from hidden to visible to allow\nthe slider handle to be fully visible when it extends beyond the track.\n\n* fix(navigation): improve active link contrast in dark mode\n\nActive navigation links now use pure white text in dark mode for\nmaximum contrast, while light mode retains the brand blue color.\n\n* fix(image): reset loading state when src changes\n\nAdded useEffect to reset loading and error states when image src prop\nchanges, ensuring proper loading indicator display for new images.\n\n* fix(skeleton): prevent inline style from overriding circle border-radius\n\nCircle variant now skips inline border-radius style to allow CSS class\nto apply 50% border-radius. Added test to verify this behavior.\n\n* fix(video): correct prop name in test\n\nFixed test to use correct prop name onVideoTimeUpdate instead of\nonTimeUpdate to match the component''s actual API.\n\n* refactor: remove Menu component\n\nRemoved Menu component as it has been replaced by other navigation\ncomponents in the library.\n\n* docs(storybook): reorganize component categories\n\nAdded story sorting order and reorganized all component stories into\nlogical categories: Getting Started, Layout, Core, Navigation, Forms,\nOverlays & Dialogs, Feedback & Status, Media, and Data Display.\n\n* refactor: remove Menu component exports from index\n\nRemoved Menu component exports after component deletion to fix\nTypeScript errors about missing module.\n\n* feat(video): improve volume slider UX with grace period\n\nAdded configurable delay (default 500ms) before hiding volume slider\nafter mouse leaves. Slider stays visible while actively dragging and\nprovides grace period for returning to adjust volume.\n\n- Added volumeSliderDelay prop to Video component\n- Implemented state management for slider visibility with timer\n- Slider remains visible during active drag interactions\n- Updated CSS to support programmatic visibility control\n- All existing tests pass\n\n* style(video): improve volume slider visibility and spacing\n\nAdded dark background and padding to volume slider when visible, and\nreduced gap between volume icon and slider for better visual grouping.\n\n* fix(audio): prevent volume slider from being clipped and improve styling\n\n- Added overflow: visible to controls, buttonGroup, and volumeControl\n  to prevent volume slider from being cut off\n- Reduced margin-bottom and padding for more compact appearance\n- Moved slider closer to volume icon for better visual proximity\n- Improved background with theme tokens and enhanced shadow\n- Reduced width from 120px to 100px for better proportions\n\n* style(audio): refine volume slider styling for dark theme\n\n- Removed vertical padding (kept horizontal only)\n- Added dark theme specific styles with darker background (85% black)\n  and subtle border (15% white) for better visual contrast\n\n* style(audio): increase volume slider horizontal padding\n\nIncreased horizontal padding from spacing-2 to spacing-4 to prevent\nslider indicator from getting too close to the edges.\n\n* feat(audio): add loop toggle control and fix CSS variables\n\n- Add loop toggle button with visual indicator (primary color when active)\n- Add state management for loop control in both single and playlist modes\n- Fix CSS variables throughout component (--boom-color-* to --boom-theme-*)\n- Update button styling to use color-only approach without backgrounds\n- Support playlist looping (restarts from first track after last track ends)\n\n* docs(audio): add visual styling to Custom Styled story\n\nAdd custom CSS decorator with pink/purple gradient theme to demonstrate\nclassName prop usage for custom theming. Previously the story had no\nvisual difference from the default story.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: resolve TypeScript and lint errors in Video and Image components\n\n- Video: Fix ref handling by using internal ref and merging with forwarded ref\n- Video: Fix PiP toggle to capture ref value before async operation\n- Image: Fix setState in useEffect with proper eslint suppression\n- VideoControls: Add eslint suppression for non-interactive div wrapper\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: resolve TypeScript type errors in FormStepper, NotificationMenu, and Video components\n\n- Add type guard function in FormStepper to properly narrow React children to FormStep elements\n- Update NotificationMenu context to accept nullable button ref\n- Update Video component refs to properly reflect nullable types\n- Remove unnecessary type assertions and simplify code\n\nThese changes fix CI type check and lint failures while maintaining type safety.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpbweICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAo2sQAJqaYinSYVx3vo8AtHScbFHV\nOM3ZFspxEtggCHR0IrU65tzy+6fBlHen2JfgznAgVp7nIPDmdTrS9XIt1bAlEf8n\ne4oQ/FDC1YXTAATDebPKvD9DQUjbZ4CApdytpNQ/YZf2owp1ev1yxLHlzF06krt8\nB7y2NuB3gkUFD+rPREPaZ069NBvxQ7glxDThMVd/UPQ/oZKmYOYox/2n13Ih7aMq\nJuIoD2ic8Z6qA20tNRlaZiRsE3eAECz/7T9C5wk0yMOq7twKtaPSWLFhEu2TPH4Z\nXXLc3OS24Cw515etP04WOSHpiy/BMuXdYTzlMsHlCFvkb1nxOT4oTdxKyXFNhlrt\nE+Nzyg+6K8Wf37QYd+i4g1Ep/7HAZefFXPeRxLHxkPQMJrU0j1K3H0fQYbU7XPNb\nQXNYvwdBMhDkQyMz7ltt6IGMNXeHVQVquAjj6vEvREOXTnZazj73r/mY0ANykD0I\nsZXlTkDzuOTPJRroJYTs37tIHN1y8uZ16v9LcS/Gh1q5jyirf1xLjvVtGYBt52ey\n6eLH+FU+HA2HmlxrCrwmHcjX6OJP27YWsdvAyXLdqM6MO6EYHt1RUyENDx5oVKFE\