boom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/whatisboom","id":123084,"login":"whatisboom","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMzA4NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whatisboom/boom-ui/commits/1a5a137f0ad599d30c1b2ea52da154ccbee07c4b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-01-20T04:07:45Z","email":"brandon@whatisboom.com","name":"Brandon Jernigan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-01-20T04:07:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(navigation): implement Breadcrumbs component (#71)\n\n* feat(navigation): implement Breadcrumbs component\n\nAdd compound component pattern for hierarchical navigation breadcrumbs with customizable separators and responsive max items collapsing.\n\nFeatures:\n- Breadcrumbs.Item compound component pattern\n- Custom separators (text or icons)\n- maxItems with ellipsis collapse\n- Polymorphic component support (as prop)\n- Proper ARIA attributes (aria-label, aria-current)\n\nAccessibility:\n- aria-label=\"breadcrumb\" on nav element\n- aria-current=\"page\" on current item\n- aria-hidden on separators and ellipsis\n- Semantic <nav> and <ol> structure\n\nTests: 28 tests, 100% coverage\nStories: 11 comprehensive examples\n\nCloses #13\n\n* fix(components): correct NotificationMenu triggerRef type\n\n* fix(breadcrumbs): export BreadcrumbItem separately for proper typing\n\n* fix(breadcrumbs): address PR review comments\n\n- Conditionally pass href only to anchor elements to prevent invalid HTML\n- Add pointer-events: none to .item.plain for consistent non-interactive behavior\n- Enforce minimum effective maxItems of 3 to ensure meaningful breadcrumb display\n- Fix NotificationMenu triggerRef type to accept null\n\n* fix(breadcrumbs): improve Fragment key stability and documentation\n\n- Extract generateItemKey() function for stable React keys\n- Use href-based keys instead of array index to prevent reconciliation issues\n- Add proper TypeScript type guards for child.props access\n- Fix href prop documentation to clarify span rendering behavior\n- Document maxItems minimum effective value of 3\n- Add comprehensive test coverage for key generation logic","tree":{"sha":"98722ba9281ce151acfe01c1d8edc0ae18318324","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whatisboom/boom-ui/git/trees/98722ba9281ce151acfe01c1d8edc0ae18318324"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whatisboom/boom-ui/git/commits/1a5a137f0ad599d30c1b2ea52da154ccbee07c4b","verification":{"payload":"tree 98722ba9281ce151acfe01c1d8edc0ae18318324\nparent b5d7d33949fc33c14f440740bcbed15a131f012a\nauthor Brandon Jernigan <brandon@whatisboom.com> 1768882065 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1768882065 +0000\n\nfeat(navigation): implement Breadcrumbs component (#71)\n\n* feat(navigation): implement Breadcrumbs component\n\nAdd compound component pattern for hierarchical navigation breadcrumbs with customizable separators and responsive max items collapsing.\n\nFeatures:\n- Breadcrumbs.Item compound component pattern\n- Custom separators (text or icons)\n- maxItems with ellipsis collapse\n- Polymorphic component support (as prop)\n- Proper ARIA attributes (aria-label, aria-current)\n\nAccessibility:\n- aria-label=\"breadcrumb\" on nav element\n- aria-current=\"page\" on current item\n- aria-hidden on separators and ellipsis\n- Semantic <nav> and <ol> structure\n\nTests: 28 tests, 100% coverage\nStories: 11 comprehensive examples\n\nCloses #13\n\n* fix(components): correct NotificationMenu triggerRef type\n\n* fix(breadcrumbs): export BreadcrumbItem separately for proper typing\n\n* fix(breadcrumbs): address PR review comments\n\n- Conditionally pass href only to anchor elements to prevent invalid HTML\n- Add pointer-events: none to .item.plain for consistent non-interactive behavior\n- Enforce minimum effective maxItems of 3 to ensure meaningful breadcrumb display\n- Fix NotificationMenu triggerRef type to accept null\n\n* fix(breadcrumbs): improve Fragment key stability and documentation\n\n- Extract generateItemKey() function for stable React keys\n- Use href-based keys instead of array index to prevent reconciliation issues\n- Add proper TypeScript type guards for child.props access\n- Fix href prop documentation to clarify span rendering behavior\n- Document maxItems minimum effective value of 3\n- Add comprehensive test coverage for key generation logic","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpbv+RCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIGAQAK6llJEL/uWbFZMc2EhGlZNp\nydS9cucnafWOWxZBAfwZzimiVBiTYRXoOTEOG+sKANhrae8MCmPYchBP69kJsmBn\nKi9F7fmuTL828AbKrsz6fGTtlAEhbet8Zj1WElBXx3c7HCNmyZtRjZdisRVRrkCO\nJgHLFkvLBtmSx4VwFGC7zNkuasbyPDbSDpZZBtqxY6WDhwxfM1IkCLTMqs9Wt5An\no/7VG38WAQc42+4uuKBJF+YNqJb+/qBuJiRx2E+9F0Lo247hEHMccsfstDQMM+1c\nM0tIXc85j0GQiNlQnYcDB6Fi6f0mdWZxDnvGsn50GOtVQ//NLJSEaRO4yttK/9mX\nACWvaMSOIAkIyvwKcLzpUJj+BxETG5LQZGz4GEk+QYSrWVPwQK4ZX/iVkwG7kSsA\nVHKQvt+cI9JhNDtpdBnx5rKDZTkI24qYwL+IlK3f0C1rSwlLPpoXGqLh2n6u48ns\nhHiXfN8bzr6/FsqQWVpIzLXnV4GtRfX1AUGfga5LHK4DUMTXx2Ud1WTgi04jQ3YS\n6WXGZlvjxy9mnKXGlZzvGnLfgBnUeQwi+JfJFEZYAhN5BsR4DNyWPBGZXfC9VroN\ndPAap3S89d0PhtJzoj7b1zGQX/0pz8dbSEfYHJmSvwRsnXsJZxzXpLruDVAx/NNG\n9xKLNYj5/ELskKOzHPQo\n=vxUq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-01-20T04:07:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whatisboom/boom-ui/commit/1a5a137f0ad599d30c1b2ea52da154ccbee07c4b","node_id":"C_kwDOQtUQc9oAKDFhNWExMzdmMGFkNTk5ZDMwYzFiMmVhNTJkYTE1NGNjYmVlMDdjNGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whatisboom/boom-ui/commit/b5d7d33949fc33c14f440740bcbed15a131f012a","sha":"b5d7d33949fc33c14f440740bcbed15a131f012a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whatisboom/boom-ui/commits/b5d7d33949fc33c14f440740bcbed15a131f012a"}],"sha":"1a5a137f0ad599d30c1b2ea52da154ccbee07c4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whatisboom/boom-ui/commits/1a5a137f0ad599d30c1b2ea52da154ccbee07c4b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/123084?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/whatisboom","id":123084,"login":"whatisboom","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMzA4NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/whatisboom","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whatisboom/boom-ui/commits/b5d7d33949fc33c14f440740bcbed15a131f012a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-01-20T03:21:30Z","email":"brandon@whatisboom.com","name":"Brandon Jernigan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-01-20T03:21:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(layout): Tier 1 components and Grid responsive enhancement (#70)\n\n* feat(layout): implement Container component\n\nAdd responsive Container component with:\n- Five size variants (sm, md, lg, xl, full)\n- Customizable padding using spacing tokens\n- Optional horizontal centering\n- Polymorphic ''as'' prop for semantic HTML\n- Full accessibility support (axe tests passing)\n- Comprehensive Storybook documentation\n- 30 test cases with 100% coverage\n\nCloses #9\n\nCo-Authored-By: Brandon Jernigan <brandon@whatisboom.com>\n\n* feat(layout): implement Divider component\n\nAdd visual separator Divider component with:\n- Horizontal and vertical orientation support\n- Three style variants (solid, dashed, dotted)\n- Optional text/icon labels for horizontal dividers\n- Label positioning (left, center, right)\n- Semantic HTML (<hr> when no label)\n- Full accessibility support (axe tests passing)\n- Comprehensive Storybook documentation\n- 32 test cases with 100% coverage\n\nCloses #10\n\nCo-Authored-By: Brandon Jernigan <brandon@whatisboom.com>\n\n* feat(layout): add responsive breakpoint support to Grid component\n\nAdd ResponsiveValue<T> type for breakpoint-based properties (base, sm, md, lg, xl). Grid now supports both simple number values and responsive object syntax for columns and gap props.\n\nFeatures:\n- columns prop accepts number or { base?, sm?, md?, lg?, xl? }\n- gap prop accepts number or { base?, sm?, md?, lg?, xl? }\n- Responsive CSS classes with media queries for all breakpoints\n- Maintains backward compatibility with existing number-only syntax\n\nTests: 40 tests, 100% coverage\nStories: Added 5 responsive layout examples\n\nCloses #8\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(grid): export GRID_BREAKPOINTS constant from main index\n\nExport GRID_BREAKPOINTS from package index to make it part of the\npublic API. Consumers using responsive Grid features can now reference\nthese breakpoint values programmatically (e.g., for matching media\nqueries in their own code).\n\n* feat(grid): add missing gap classes and export GRID_BREAKPOINTS\n\n- Add gap classes for spacing tokens 5, 10, 16, 20 across all breakpoints\n- Export GRID_BREAKPOINTS constant from main package index\n- Ensures all spacing system tokens are supported for responsive gaps\n\nThis allows responsive gap values like gap={{ base: 5, md: 10, lg: 20 }}\nto work correctly.\n\n* feat(grid): add fallback for empty responsive objects\n\nAdd default values when empty responsive objects are provided:\n- columns={{}} now defaults to gridTemplateColumns: ''1fr''\n- gap={{}} now defaults to gap: ''var(--boom-spacing-4)''\n\nThis prevents grids with no column/gap definition when users pass\nempty responsive objects. Includes tests for both edge cases.\n\nAddresses Copilot feedback on PR #70.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4949227b23b5e20545f9f8eebf5c06fbd709d32e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whatisboom/boom-ui/git/trees/4949227b23b5e20545f9f8eebf5c06fbd709d32e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whatisboom/boom-ui/git/commits/b5d7d33949fc33c14f440740bcbed15a131f012a","verification":{"payload":"tree 4949227b23b5e20545f9f8eebf5c06fbd709d32e\nparent f75320b12b213774efef9b065a7b0bb7287b995c\nauthor Brandon Jernigan <brandon@whatisboom.com> 1768879290 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1768879290 -0600\n\nfeat(layout): Tier 1 components and Grid responsive enhancement (#70)\n\n* feat(layout): implement Container component\n\nAdd responsive Container component with:\n- Five size variants (sm, md, lg, xl, full)\n- Customizable padding using spacing tokens\n- Optional horizontal centering\n- Polymorphic ''as'' prop for semantic HTML\n- Full accessibility support (axe tests passing)\n- Comprehensive Storybook documentation\n- 30 test cases with 100% coverage\n\nCloses #9\n\nCo-Authored-By: Brandon Jernigan <brandon@whatisboom.com>\n\n* feat(layout): implement Divider component\n\nAdd visual separator Divider component with:\n- Horizontal and vertical orientation support\n- Three style variants (solid, dashed, dotted)\n- Optional text/icon labels for horizontal dividers\n- Label positioning (left, center, right)\n- Semantic HTML (<hr> when no label)\n- Full accessibility support (axe tests passing)\n- Comprehensive Storybook documentation\n- 32 test cases with 100% coverage\n\nCloses #10\n\nCo-Authored-By: Brandon Jernigan <brandon@whatisboom.com>\n\n* feat(layout): add responsive breakpoint support to Grid component\n\nAdd ResponsiveValue<T> type for breakpoint-based properties (base, sm, md, lg, xl). Grid now supports both simple number values and responsive object syntax for columns and gap props.\n\nFeatures:\n- columns prop accepts number or { base?, sm?, md?, lg?, xl? }\n- gap prop accepts number or { base?, sm?, md?, lg?, xl? }\n- Responsive CSS classes with media queries for all breakpoints\n- Maintains backward compatibility with existing number-only syntax\n\nTests: 40 tests, 100% coverage\nStories: Added 5 responsive layout examples\n\nCloses #8\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(grid): export GRID_BREAKPOINTS constant from main index\n\nExport GRID_BREAKPOINTS from package index to make it part of the\npublic API. Consumers using responsive Grid features can now reference\nthese breakpoint values programmatically (e.g., for matching media\nqueries in their own code).\n\n* feat(grid): add missing gap classes and export GRID_BREAKPOINTS\n\n- Add gap classes for spacing tokens 5, 10, 16, 20 across all breakpoints\n- Export GRID_BREAKPOINTS constant from main package index\n- Ensures all spacing system tokens are supported for responsive gaps\n\nThis allows responsive gap values like gap={{ base: 5, md: 10, lg: 20 }}\nto work correctly.\n\n* feat(grid): add fallback for empty responsive objects\n\nAdd default values when empty responsive objects are provided:\n- columns={{}} now defaults to gridTemplateColumns: ''1fr''\n- gap={{}} now defaults to gap: ''var(--boom-spacing-4)''\n\nThis prevents grids with no column/gap definition when users pass\nempty responsive objects. Includes tests for both edge cases.\n\nAddresses Copilot feedback on PR #70.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpbvS6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbYQQAEDvA7DTduZAnjyZkLD67BGz\nSAA06XfnzrUgqB8NTaKvVnvx18wp5cPk6WMizWJTHMSGhJGOntx/Wl5oYv72XPVV\n1DCaTTQywoBkAeWDRMmz+MI8bdxnR6cFQSFkFo+QDBOopepy476AxtnIWoZU4bBA\nPeTs91kn/aH+aKQSneujaAZTNuA5bHuO+76rGasUXHaW7ah2SG/DrZR/yY11tbWz\njay+rWlN/M3s942NG3wneKt6OLR3nR1pPhSvH6tExA9rnLMvzJ7+lSWwm12HNeQQ\n1BHrELTUuHrvyOUr+FJATSSzMIAu0cqXYdRdwghRNWFOP1GIppWSMoLz/H7ia9J7\n7qigBRNfH4hcb7nOrz7vcWZ/R4UFfVSsZIpt8xBuXReNgnFH0mKGxBQ0pRR/nPmM\nSmxSMXFgkBilYACas6kKCKj3gJr8qachFxFf96Vt95NOjT2tbw2pAQRuc6c+P9V5\ngIh7ednM8fHqqbjrt0N0OkuQrdbWJ29C1Z8YtHTa7XrkBc62DTmGJZDPxC33C4P4\nVg3mPmNlmEU1lCQDYc7fHhHoT/Y3g2Ln9Ad8O/LBCWl/gUHWfi6XYGbIXvImsTWY\nOH6UP+SEEYbaCr8AjUhlQxHnPMe+tjKS2z0u7lvBYhHB79hBZAigYP0RKmFbiwE/\n9jM65E1gnatCFigzsgDP\n=dBvo\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-01-20T03:21:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubuserconte