ZTU1NjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commit/6624827c7d9643c0aa68f66e9f93d441e8c5c9ee","sha":"6624827c7d9643c0aa68f66e9f93d441e8c5c9ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commits/6624827c7d9643c0aa68f66e9f93d441e8c5c9ee"}],"sha":"6bfdf02c2f6fd6858e89672de5fc4fee5e8e5561","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commits/6bfdf02c2f6fd6858e89672de5fc4fee5e8e5561"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/101348966?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17","id":101348966,"login":"tt-tom17","node_id":"U_kgDOBgp2Zg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commits/6624827c7d9643c0aa68f66e9f93d441e8c5c9ee/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T01:16:01Z","email":"tgb@kabelmail.de","name":"tt-tom17"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T11:49:39Z","email":"tgb@kabelmail.de","name":"tt-tom17"},"message":"fix: take walking times from the TRIAS time window and drop past trips\n\nThree defects that only showed up once real journeys were polled, all measured\nagainst efa-bw.de/trias on 2026-08-25 with Karlsruhe West -> Baden-Baden\nKurhaus.\n\nWalking legs had no times at all. The mapper read ServiceDeparture and\nServiceArrival, which belong to a TimedLeg and are never present on a\nContinuousLeg. The measurement shows where the times live: TimeWindowStart,\nTimeWindowEnd, Duration and Length, and an InterchangeLeg carries WalkDuration\nand BufferTime on top. Length now fills the distance field FPTF provides for\nwalking legs, and the types were extended to match the measurement.\n\nAs a consequence a journey that starts or ends on foot had neither departure\nnor arrival, and journeys.ts wrote DurationMinutes = -1, because it derives\nboth from legs[0].departure and the last leg''s arrival. With the times in\nplace that resolves itself; Trip/StartTime and Trip/EndTime are now used as a\nfallback for the edges, so a leg without a time window cannot break it again.\n\nThe server also answers a request for \"now\" with trips that have already\ndeparted: three of thirteen at night, one of seven during the day. Cutting the\nlist to the requested count therefore filled the first slots with yesterday''s\nconnections. Past trips are dropped before the cut; a trip without a usable\nstart time is kept rather than silently discarded.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9d0c77420863e5c5026bdd30f16a58b9275018fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/git/trees/9d0c77420863e5c5026bdd30f16a58b9275018fb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/git/commits/6624827c7d9643c0aa68f66e9f93d441e8c5c9ee","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/101348966?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17","id":101348966,"login":"tt-tom17","node_id":"U_kgDOBgp2Zg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commit/6624827c7d9643c0aa68f66e9f93d441e8c5c9ee","node_id":"C_kwDOQuA_-NoAKDY2MjQ4MjdjN2Q5NjQzYzBhYTY4ZjY2ZTlmOTNkNDQxZThjNWM5ZWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commit/5d84edb3c8d426b9c2c896dcb5122b52143212a5","sha":"5d84edb3c8d426b9c2c896dcb5122b52143212a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commits/5d84edb3c8d426b9c2c896dcb5122b52143212a5"}],"sha":"6624827c7d9643c0aa68f66e9f93d441e8c5c9ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commits/6624827c7d9643c0aa68f66e9f93d441e8c5c9ee"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/101348966?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17","id":101348966,"login":"tt-tom17","node_id":"U_kgDOBgp2Zg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commits/5d84edb3c8d426b9c2c896dcb5122b52143212a5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T00:41:20Z","email":"tgb@kabelmail.de","name":"tt-tom17"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T11:49:39Z","email":"tgb@kabelmail.de","name":"tt-tom17"},"message":"fix: treat \"nothing found\" from TRIAS as an empty result, not an error\n\nTRIAS has no empty answer: instead of an empty result list the server sends an\nErrorMessage. Until now every one of them without results was thrown, so a\nstation that simply has no departures produced an error plus a warning on every\npoll. Measured on 2026-08-25 against efa-bw.de/trias: Freiburg im Breisgau Bad\n(de:08311:30605) answers -4030 at 02:30 with a 60 minute window, while the same\nrequest with 480 minutes returns ten departures. At night that turns the log\ninto a wall of errors for a service that works.\n\nFour codes now count as an empty result and are logged at debug level: -4030\n(no departures), -4000 (no trip at the requested time) and -8014 / -8020 (the\nlocation search has no match, which happens with every keystroke in the admin\nUI). This mirrors what the HAFAS backend already does for H890. A code that is\nnot on the list still throws, and it only applies when every message in the\nanswer is harmless, so a real failure next to a -4030 is not swallowed.\n\nThe adapter then reaches the empty-result path it already had, which says \"No\ndepartures found for station ...\". That line now also names the time window,\nbecause it is the usual explanation, and the German fragment in the otherwise\nEnglish message is gone.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"538f3ad3c774ad2aa499f851fcaabe53716a1d42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/git/trees/538f3ad3c774ad2aa499f851fcaabe53716a1d42"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/git/commits/5d84edb3c8d426b9c2c896dcb5122b52143212a5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/101348966?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17","id":101348966,"login":"tt-tom17","node_id":"U_kgDOBgp2Zg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commit/5d84edb3c8d426b9c2c896dcb5122b52143212a5","node_id":"C_kwDOQuA_-NoAKDVkODRlZGIzYzhkNDI2YjljMmM4OTZkY2I1MTIyYjUyMTQzMjEyYTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commit/56f35d86bbf6a9a71db1fd2115c729380f975dd0","sha":"56f35d86bbf6a9a71db1fd2115c729380f975dd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commits/56f35d86bbf6a9a71db1fd2115c729380f975dd0"}],"sha":"5d84edb3c8d426b9c2c896dcb5122b52143212a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commits/5d84edb3c8d426b9c2c896dcb5122b52143212a5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/101348966?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17","id":101348966,"login":"tt-tom17","node_id":"U_kgDOBgp2Zg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commits/56f35d86bbf6a9a71db1fd2115c729380f975dd0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T00:17:52Z","email":"tgb@kabelmail.de","name":"tt-tom17"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T11:49:39Z","email":"tgb@kabelmail.de","name":"tt-tom17"},"message":"docs: describe the TRIAS access key, the NVBW attribution and the clients used\n\nWithout the application instructions the TRIAS backend is unusable: providers\nissue the RequestorRef per user, and the adapter cannot ship a shared key. The\ndata sources section now says how to request one for MobiData BW and which\nfield it goes into.\n\nMobiData BW also requires the source to be credited as \"Daten der NVBW\" with a\nlink, in the documentation as well as in the user interface. The instance\nsettings already carried it, the README did not. Unlike the VRR no logo is\nasked for, so the paragraph goes after the float of the VRR logo instead of\nnext to it.\n\nThe section also names the clients the queries are built with, hafas-client\nand motis-fptf-client, because the adapter only owns the EFA and TRIAS\nimplementations and the rest of the work is done by those projects.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b9d873c96f656e91372a931e1fb446e9bffa384c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/git/trees/b9d873c96f656e91372a931e1fb446e9bffa384c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/git/commits/56f35d86bbf6a9a71db1fd2115c729380f975dd0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/101348966?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17","id":101348966,"login":"tt-tom17","node_id":"U_kgDOBgp2Zg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commit/56f35d86bbf6a9a71db1fd2115c729380f975dd0","node_id":"C_kwDOQuA_-NoAKDU2ZjM1ZDg2YmJmNmE5YTcxZGIxZmQyMTE1YzcyOTM4MGY5NzVkZDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commit/5ac47ae04101d14543a71849d26dd2154556781c","sha":"5ac47ae04101d14543a71849d26dd2154556781c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commits/5ac47ae04101d14543a71849d26dd2154556781c"}],"sha":"56f35d86bbf6a9a71db1fd2115c729380f975dd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commits/56f35d86bbf6a9a71db1fd2115c729380f975dd0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/101348966?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17","id":101348966,"login":"tt-tom17","node_id":"U_kgDOBgp2Zg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commits/5ac47ae04101d14543a71849d26dd2154556781c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T00:12:40Z","email":"tgb@kabelmail.de","name":"tt-tom17"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T11:49:39Z","email":"tgb@kabelmail.de","name":"tt-tom17"},"message":"feat: keep the TRIAS requestor ref encrypted and out of foreign adapters\n\nThe requestor ref is a personal access secret, so it must not sit in the\ninstance configuration in plain text. Adding it to encryptedNative makes the\ncontroller store it encrypted and hand it to the adapter decrypted, and\nprotectedNative keeps it from being served to other adapters that read this\ninstance object.\n\nBoth lists belong on the top level of io-package.json, next to native, not\nbelow common: the controller reads obj.encryptedNative and obj.protectedNative\nfrom the instance object itself. Every installed adapter that guards a secret\ndoes it the same way, among them backitup, influxdb and javascript.\n\nThe admin UI still shows the value, because admin is exempt from the protection\nfilter (NO_PROTECT_ADAPTERS). A key that was already saved in plain text has to\nbe entered once more, since it is now read as an encrypted value.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5f520c298aa4702368a46c6605ef25901f0e3db9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/git/trees/5f520c298aa4702368a46c6605ef25901f0e3db9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/git/commits/5ac47ae04101d14543a71849d26dd2154556781c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/101348966?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17","id":101348966,"login":"tt-tom17","node_id":"U_kgDOBgp2Zg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commit/5ac47ae04101d14543a71849d26dd2154556781c","node_id":"C_kwDOQuA_-NoAKDVhYzQ3YWUwNDEwMWQxNDU0M2E3MTg0OWQyNmRkMjE1NDU1Njc4MWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commit/aa1b0e9ad08aa2c69593eb5e64c362afe78f5bca","sha":"aa1b0e9ad08aa2c69593eb5e64c362afe78f5bca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commits/aa1b0e9ad08aa2c69593eb5e64c362afe78f5bca"}],"sha":"5ac47ae04101d14543a71849d26dd2154556781c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commits/5ac47ae04101d14543a71849d26dd2154556781c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/101348966?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17","id":101348966,"login":"tt-tom17","node_id":"U_kgDOBgp2Zg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commits/aa1b0e9ad08aa2c69593eb5e64c362afe78f5bca/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T16:33:06Z","email":"tgb@kabelmail.de","name":"tt-tom17"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T11:49:39Z","email":"tgb@kabelmail.de","name":"tt-tom17"},"message":"feat: add TRIAS as a new backend with MobiData BW as the first network\n\nTRIAS (VDV 431-2 v1.2) is an XML interface used by several German transport\nauthorities. As with EFA there is no ready-made client in the hafas-client\nformat, so TriasService builds a shim and triasMapper translates the responses\ninto FPTF. Requests are derived from the schema rather than from sample files,\nbecause the parameters live in xs:sequence and their order is mandatory.\n\nUnlike every other backend TRIAS needs an access key per user, so the settings\ngained a password field. The key never reaches the log: the request body is\nmasked before it is written.\n\nThe vehicle mapping comes from the VDV enumeration instead of a sample, which\nkeeps it valid for a second TRIAS provider. Measured against efa-bw.de on\n2026-08-24, all nine mode combinations the server returns are covered by it.\n\nThree findings from that measurement are encoded in the code and the tests:\n- Service attributes carry a Code as well, with values such as FK, 1 and 28,\n  so errors are recognised by path and never by the shape of the value\n- the product filter needs an explicit Exclude=false, otherwise it silently\n  turns into an exclusion list\n- line and mode live below ServiceSection, not directly below Service\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"56a13f89feb2cde21b28d7180ffc28807bce4760","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/git/trees/56a13f89feb2cde21b28d7180ffc28807bce4760"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/git/commits/aa1b0e9ad08aa2c69593eb5e64c362afe78f5bca","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/101348966?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/