url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commits/8e3c3b467fd201ce6625fc5e1eb4ca7171170195/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T22:53:24Z","email":"tgb@kabelmail.de","name":"tt-tom17"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T09:54:24Z","email":"tgb@kabelmail.de","name":"tt-tom17"},"message":"feat: tie the EFA endpoint to the network and show the VRR attribution\n\nThe EFA base URL was a free text field in the instance settings. It now belongs to the\nselected network (EFA_NETWORKS in EfaService), resolved from the profile the same way\nHafasService resolves its profile object. The reason is the terms of use rather than\nconvenience: the VRR grants access to its Open Service API under conditions that the\nadapter fulfils on behalf of every user, and a freely entered third-party server would\nquietly undermine that agreement. Another EFA network is therefore a code change after\nits terms have been settled, not a setting.\n\nIn place of the removed field the settings tab now carries what the VRR asks for: its\nlogo next to a link to www.vrr.de. The hint is bound to the vrr profile, not merely to\nthe efa service type, so a future second EFA network cannot inherit the wrong logo.\n\nThe logo is embedded as an inline SVG component instead of an imported file. The admin\nbuild runs tsc before vite, and src-admin/tsconfig.json does not include vite/client,\nso an asset import would fail type checking; a relative image path would also not be\nreliably resolvable inside the module federation bundle. The path data is taken from\nthe file the VRR supplied, generated rather than retyped.\n\nTwo consequences worth naming:\n\n- clientProfile now validates the profile part for EFA as well. It was skipped because\n  only the configured base URL decided the region for EFA - that reasoning no longer\n  holds once the profile selects the network and with it the endpoint.\n- The compiled EFA modules were never committed, although build/ is tracked otherwise.\n  build/lib/class/efaService.js and build/lib/tools/efaMapper.js are added here, so a\n  checkout of this branch is complete again.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"676e73c47e3f5aae7a0ed0d27909b07a594ce107","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/git/trees/676e73c47e3f5aae7a0ed0d27909b07a594ce107"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/git/commits/8e3c3b467fd201ce6625fc5e1eb4ca7171170195","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/101348966?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17","id":101348966,"login":"tt-tom17","node_id":"U_kgDOBgp2Zg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commit/8e3c3b467fd201ce6625fc5e1eb4ca7171170195","node_id":"C_kwDOQuA_-NoAKDhlM2MzYjQ2N2ZkMjAxY2U2NjI1ZmM1ZTFlYjRjYTcxNzExNzAxOTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commit/1d6ca90c5f95e51408553dc83bd502c1ad42441a","sha":"1d6ca90c5f95e51408553dc83bd502c1ad42441a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commits/1d6ca90c5f95e51408553dc83bd502c1ad42441a"}],"sha":"8e3c3b467fd201ce6625fc5e1eb4ca7171170195","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commits/8e3c3b467fd201ce6625fc5e1eb4ca7171170195"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/101348966?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17","id":101348966,"login":"tt-tom17","node_id":"U_kgDOBgp2Zg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commits/1d6ca90c5f95e51408553dc83bd502c1ad42441a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T23:52:30Z","email":"tgb@kabelmail.de","name":"tt-tom17"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T09:54:13Z","email":"tgb@kabelmail.de","name":"tt-tom17"},"message":"fix: load the language files from their current location again\n\nThe lookup still pointed at admin/i18n/<lang>/translations.json, but those files were\nreplaced by the flat admin/i18n/<lang>.json during the admin 8 migration. Since then\nno language file was found at all: the adapter warned once per supported language and\ngetTranslationObj() returned every key unchanged, so object names were no longer\ntranslated. getTranslation() only kept working because it falls back to the custom\nfile, which does still exist.\n\nThe files are now read with readFileSync instead of a dynamic JSON import. That import\nbehaves differently per module system - it becomes a require in the built CommonJS, but\nunder ts-node it needs an import attribute and throws without one, which is why a unit\ntest could not have caught this before. Reading the file works the same in both worlds.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"36cf7e2cfe727957e3c9bf18288dfe6c924e3a0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/git/trees/36cf7e2cfe727957e3c9bf18288dfe6c924e3a0c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/git/commits/1d6ca90c5f95e51408553dc83bd502c1ad42441a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/101348966?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17","id":101348966,"login":"tt-tom17","node_id":"U_kgDOBgp2Zg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commit/1d6ca90c5f95e51408553dc83bd502c1ad42441a","node_id":"C_kwDOQuA_-NoAKDFkNmNhOTBjNWY5NWU1MTQwODU1M2RjODNiZDUwMmMxYWQ0MjQ0MWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commit/7f8901d78610bf0d135aeb3f45e5c4a6e4b510dc","sha":"7f8901d78610bf0d135aeb3f45e5c4a6e4b510dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commits/7f8901d78610bf0d135aeb3f45e5c4a6e4b510dc"}],"sha":"1d6ca90c5f95e51408553dc83bd502c1ad42441a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commits/1d6ca90c5f95e51408553dc83bd502c1ad42441a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/101348966?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17","id":101348966,"login":"tt-tom17","node_id":"U_kgDOBgp2Zg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commits/7f8901d78610bf0d135aeb3f45e5c4a6e4b510dc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T23:32:53Z","email":"tgb@kabelmail.de","name":"tt-tom17"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T09:52:43Z","email":"tgb@kabelmail.de","name":"tt-tom17"},"message":"test: cover the EFA mapper with unit tests\n\nPins the three behaviours that only showed up against the live endpoint: a footpath\ncarries MOT class 99 (and a transportation block, so it must not be detected by a\nmissing one), a transfer walk is only a leg of its own when the server does not\nalready account for it, and productClasses may sit below assignedStops. Also covers\nthe delay calculation, both cancellation flavours and the platform/trip number\nfields that FPTF expects in specific places.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"28bd51d8e526bbd63670375bce8357867322d20a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/git/trees/28bd51d8e526bbd63670375bce8357867322d20a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/git/commits/7f8901d78610bf0d135aeb3f45e5c4a6e4b510dc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/101348966?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17","id":101348966,"login":"tt-tom17","node_id":"U_kgDOBgp2Zg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commit/7f8901d78610bf0d135aeb3f45e5c4a6e4b510dc","node_id":"C_kwDOQuA_-NoAKDdmODkwMWQ3ODYxMGJmMGQxMzVhZWIzZjQ1ZTVjNGE2ZTRiNTEwZGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commit/1f41fb848bf52c06277d832438f69b4566aa3bd6","sha":"1f41fb848bf52c06277d832438f69b4566aa3bd6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commits/1f41fb848bf52c06277d832438f69b4566aa3bd6"}],"sha":"7f8901d78610bf0d135aeb3f45e5c4a6e4b510dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commits/7f8901d78610bf0d135aeb3f45e5c4a6e4b510dc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/101348966?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17","id":101348966,"login":"tt-tom17","node_id":"U_kgDOBgp2Zg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commits/1f41fb848bf52c06277d832438f69b4566aa3bd6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T23:25:38Z","email":"tgb@kabelmail.de","name":"tt-tom17"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T09:52:43Z","email":"tgb@kabelmail.de","name":"tt-tom17"},"message":"feat: add EFA as a new backend with VRR as the first network\n\nEFA (Mentz, outputFormat=rapidJSON) has no hafas-client compatible package, so\nEfaService builds a shim instead: createClient() returns an object that issues the\nthree EFA requests (stop finder, departure monitor, trip) and maps the responses to\nFPTF via efaMapper. Timeout, retries and product sanitizing stay in\nBaseTransportService, so the rest of the adapter sees no difference to HAFAS,\ndb-vendo or MOTIS.\n\nVerified against the live VRR endpoint. Three findings are handled explicitly:\n- footpaths carry product.class 99 instead of no transportation at all, so checking\n  for a missing transportation block would list them as rides\n- the server sorts by planned time, but reports planned 00:00 with an estimated time\n  hours later for night express lines; departures are therefore sorted by the actual\n  time and the time window is applied to it as well\n- when looking up a location by id, productClasses is only present below\n  assignedStops\n\nThe product filter is applied after mapping because EFA implements it per network.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c6853fae75d64f8079f843d37b9c3a279d032e34","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/git/trees/c6853fae75d64f8079f843d37b9c3a279d032e34"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/git/commits/1f41fb848bf52c06277d832438f69b4566aa3bd6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/101348966?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17","id":101348966,"login":"tt-tom17","node_id":"U_kgDOBgp2Zg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commit/1f41fb848bf52c06277d832438f69b4566aa3bd6","node_id":"C_kwDOQuA_-NoAKDFmNDFmYjg0OGJmNTJjMDYyNzdkODMyNDM4ZjY5YjQ1NjZhYTNiZDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commit/2df6d97d01af2a9dd430a9a0f653715550282554","sha":"2df6d97d01af2a9dd430a9a0f653715550282554","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commits/2df6d97d01af2a9dd430a9a0f653715550282554"}],"sha":"1f41fb848bf52c06277d832438f69b4566aa3bd6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commits/1f41fb848bf52c06277d832438f69b4566aa3bd6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/101348966?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17","id":101348966,"login":"tt-tom17","node_id":"U_kgDOBgp2Zg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBrok