github.com/users/tt-tom17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17","id":101348966,"login":"tt-tom17","node_id":"U_kgDOBgp2Zg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/ioBroker.public-transport/commits/4ab147c88d3528607149ba6c7e4bc6e7707a915c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T08:04:10Z","email":"tgb@kabelmail.de","name":"tt-tom17"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T08:04:10Z","email":"tgb@kabelmail.de","name":"tt-tom17"},"message":"fix: keep data points written during slow polls (#87)\n\ngarbageColleting compared each state timestamp against the current time minus a\n2000 ms offset. Writing a full set of departures takes longer than that against\nslow backends, so the states written first were classified as stale and reset\nimmediately after the very poll that wrote them. Reported for a station with 20\ndepartures, where Departures_00..11 were cleared while 12..19 survived; a second\nstation in the same run wrote its 18 departures in 1.8 s and stayed intact.\n\nTake a cut-off timestamp before the write batch and pass it to garbageColleting,\nso only states the current poll did not touch are reset. Journeys use the same\ncall pattern and write even more states per poll, so they get the same fix.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"26cbc008f270cd9e5dfa903b2b4e20906d1c6963","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-tom17/i